{"author": "claude(vm-gce hd2-feats-003)", "cache_id": "gs://market-data-0998ac51/research_runs/maker_labels/{SYM}.npz ; HPs from research_runs/xgb_maker/{A_{SYM},B_pool}.json ; result research_runs/xgb_maker/WALKFORWARD.json", "commission_loss_pct": 0.02, "commission_win_pct": 0.02, "data_source": "cryptolake", "date_range_end": "2026-05-08", "date_range_start": "2025-05-09", "embargo": "expanding-window day-index folds: test windows tile fracs 0.62->1.0 in 4 steps, val=7% before each test, train=0..val; label horizon 60s", "ev_per_trade_pct": null, "experiment_id": "xgb-20260531_makerlabels_walkforward", "fee_regime": "MAKER_FIRST", "git_commit": "7250ffc2a52a104978e1666344ffb7eec20bee72", "hypothesis_id": "HD3", "kind": "strategy", "label_def": "Same as xgb-20260531_makerlabels_AB. OOS metric = executed NET maker EV(bp) over filled-chosen, op-point (cfg,qm) chosen on VAL@A-top1%, EV curve over A-selectivity measured on TEST.", "model_family": "xgboost_cascade2_maker_labels", "n_samples": 6902754, "n_trades": 0, "note": "OOS CONFIRMATION of the single-split argmax (LTC +2.0bp / LINK +1.2bp). RESULT: the positive argmax DOES NOT survive when (cfg,qm,selectivity) are chosen out-of-sample. Mean test-EV(bp) by A-selectivity top-5/2/1/0.5/0.2%: BTC -4.9/-5.0/-5.1/-5.3/-5.4; ETH -5.1/-5.3/-5.4/-5.6/-5.7; BNB -5.2/../-6.3; SOL -5.4/../-5.8; DOGE -5.9/../-3.1; XRP -5.5/../-3.4; LTC -5.3/../-2.7. 7/8 symbols STABLE NET-NEGATIVE every fold (BTC/ETH ~-5bp each fold, dir_acc ~0.50-0.51). LINK mean APPEARS positive (+6.8 @top1%, +23.9 @top0.2%) but is driven ENTIRELY by fold 0 (earliest OOS window: +38.9/+95.3bp, n=1896/375) while folds 1/2/3 are ~0/negative (top1% +0.1/-6.4/-5.6) -> a single-fold REGIME spike, NOT a stable edge (LINK also has least data: 244d incl 119d outage). CONCLUSION: the maker-realistic XGBoost cascade does NOT confirm a deployable positive maker edge OOS; the single-split +2/+1.2bp was selection-over-conditions optimism (max over ~30 cells on test) + small-sample noise at top-0.2%. Binding loss = adverse selection on PASSIVE MAKER fills, not model quality (vol-gate AUC 0.82-0.86 and dir-acc 0.66-0.77 are real). Corroborates RESEARCH_LOG s14 (passive maker entry flips edge negative; positive only with TAKER entry, +5.6bp). Next lever is EXECUTION (taker/alt mechanics), not more boosting.", "params": {"A_sel_grid_pct": [5, 2, 1, 0.5, 0.2], "B_cfg_trained": "hold-60s/qm1", "folds": 4, "hp_reuse": true, "min_n_val": 100, "nf_rate": 0.05, "seed": 0, "select_selectivity": "A-top1%"}, "repro_cmd": "python3 subs60_xgb_walkforward.py --symbols ALL --folds 4 --seed 0", "setup": "Walk-forward OOS confirmation of xgb-20260531_makerlabels_AB argmax cells: expanding-window, 4 folds; per fold the operating point (cfg,qm) is SELECTED on a VAL slice (best executed maker-EV @ A-top1%) and the EV curve MEASURED on a later disjoint TEST slice; HPs reused from the single-split run (no per-fold Optuna).", "split_method": "walkforward_7525", "status": "exploratory", "supersedes": null, "symbols": ["BNB-USDT-PERP", "BTC-USDT-PERP", "DOGE-USDT-PERP", "ETH-USDT-PERP", "LINK-USDT-PERP", "LTC-USDT-PERP", "SOL-USDT-PERP", "XRP-USDT-PERP"], "ts": "2026-05-31T10:10:00Z"}
{"author": "claude(vm-gce hd2-feats-003)", "cache_id": "gs://market-data-0998ac51/research_runs/maker_labels/{SYM}.npz ; HP/thr from research_runs/xgb_maker/{A_{SYM},B_pool}.json ; result research_runs/xgb_maker/RECENCY.json", "commission_loss_pct": 0.02, "commission_win_pct": 0.02, "data_source": "cryptolake", "date_range_end": "2026-05-08", "date_range_start": "2025-05-09", "embargo": "fixed test [0.68,1.0) day-index; train windows vary; gap to test >=0.03 ndays; label horizon 60s", "ev_per_trade_pct": null, "experiment_id": "xgb-20260531_makerlabels_recency", "fee_regime": "MAKER_FIRST", "git_commit": "32660f655a70bec97af0f8d03f27e9c44f9b068b", "hypothesis_id": "HD3", "kind": "strategy", "label_def": "Same as xgb-20260531_makerlabels_AB; per-symbol A vol-threshold FIXED to the main run's vol_thr_bp (label held constant across windows).", "model_family": "xgboost_cascade2_maker_labels", "n_samples": 6902754, "n_trades": 0, "note": "RECENCY / regime-drift DIAGNOSTIC (tests hypothesis: single-split test degradation is market DRIFT not HP overfit). Mean over 8 symbols on the SAME clean test, fixed HP/rounds/threshold, varying only the training window: old10 AUC 0.835 prec@.2% 0.463 cascEV@1% -6.17 ; val10 0.838/0.453/-6.54 ; train 0.846/0.536/-5.12 ; trainval 0.847/0.534/-5.10. RESULT: recency hypothesis NOT supported. At EQUAL size, the most-recent slice (val10, adjacent to test) ~= the oldest slice (old10, ~0.58 history away): mean dAUC(val10-old10)=+0.003 (within noise; per-symbol +0.012 LINK .. -0.006 DOGE, sign-inconsistent), no consistent maker-EV recency benefit. What clearly helps is DATA VOLUME: train/trainval (55-65% of days) beat both 10% windows on EVERY symbol (AUC +0.01-0.03, prec@.2% 0.53 vs 0.46, cascEV ~-5.1 vs -6.2bp); adding recent val to train (trainval vs train) ~=0 gain. => the model trained on year-old data generalizes to the distant test ~as well as recent data; the val>test gap is explained by operating-point selection optimism (confirmed via walk-forward) + volume/coverage, NOT non-stationarity. Implication: daily rolling-retrain (RESEARCH_LOG s14 staleness fix) likely helps THIS model little; volume matters more than freshness. Caveat: maker-EV is net-negative everywhere (adverse-selection floor) so AUC/prec are the cleaner read; single seed. Lone mild recency signal = LINK (least/gappiest data).", "params": {"cascade_eval_cell": "hold-60s/touch", "fixed_rounds": true, "fixed_threshold": true, "hp_reuse": true, "seed": 0, "test": [0.68, 1.0], "windows": {"old10": [0.0, 0.0975], "train": [0.0, 0.5525], "trainval": [0.0, 0.65], "val10": [0.5525, 0.65]}}, "repro_cmd": "python3 subs60_xgb_recency.py --symbols ALL --seed 0", "setup": "Recency/regime-drift diagnostic: hold HP + num_boost_round + per-symbol vol-threshold FIXED (reused from xgb-20260531_makerlabels_AB), vary ONLY the training-data window, measure on the SAME clean test [0.68,1.0). Windows old10[0,0.0975] train[0,0.5525] val10[0.5525,0.65] trainval[0,0.65]; old10 vs val10 are equal-size -> isolates recency from volume. No early-stop (fixed rounds) -> no eval set -> no leakage.", "split_method": "honest_val_test", "status": "exploratory", "supersedes": null, "symbols": ["BNB-USDT-PERP", "BTC-USDT-PERP", "DOGE-USDT-PERP", "ETH-USDT-PERP", "LINK-USDT-PERP", "LTC-USDT-PERP", "SOL-USDT-PERP", "XRP-USDT-PERP"], "ts": "2026-05-31T10:40:00Z"}
