(a MISS already pays 0, abstaining changes nothing). What abstention NEEDS -- 1{filled maker trade loses} -- is ~the direction sign on B's side, which is unpredictable (B dir-AUC ~0.51). So the predictable part of adverse selection is non-actionable and the actionable part is unpredictable => adverse selection cannot be cleaned by selection/prediction on these windows (corroborates the B-training-universe result: 5% optimal, direction is the wall). REMAINING lever is MECHANICAL (maker placement: offset/queue/patience; realistic resting-maker exit), not predictive. CAVEAT: 2 symbols, single split, single seed, not walk-forward; EV(top-f) curves stop at f=0.10 (not the 1/day extreme where positive EV lives) but abstAUC~random is decisive. All weights+preds persisted (cache_id).", "params": {"abstain_optuna_trials": 25, "fracs_retained": [1.0, 0.5, 0.25, 0.1], "kfolds_oof_A": 5, "nf_rate": 0.05, "reused_models": ["b_universe/A_{SYM}.xgb.json", "b_universe/B_{SYM}_g5.xgb.json"], "seed": 0}, "repro_cmd": "python3 subs60_xgb_abstain.py --symbols BTC LINK --trials 25", "setup": "Smarter-maker lever B: TOXICITY-GATED ABSTENTION -- stay maker (4bp), SKIP predicted-adverse passive fills (no taker, no fee wall). Reuses SAVED A_{SYM}.xgb.json + optimal B_{SYM}_g5.xgb.json from research_runs/b_universe (no retrain); trains ONLY a new abstention XGB (Optuna 25 trials) whose target on train (apred-5% A-non-flat, better-maker-side filled windows) is y_adv=1{maker pnl < 0}. EVAL on the FIXED A-top-5% test pool (B's side): EV(top-f) of trades retained by ranking on (a) B-confidence |pB-0.5|, (b) benign=1-P(adv), (c) combo -- does the adverse-fill predictor add orthogonal value over B-confidence?", "split_method": "honest_val_test", "status": "exploratory", "supersedes": null, "symbols": ["BTC-USDT-PERP", "LINK-USDT-PERP"], "ts": "2026-06-02T11:20:00Z"}
