ST-fill 60s outcome (near-random here, see abstain row). So C's strong fill signal was not actionable as a deploy SELECTION factor on these conditions. NOT a general claim -- untested: C as input to PLACEMENT (maker-offset/aggressiveness/queue), other deploy operating points, sequence/longer-context features, other horizons. Weights+preds persisted (cache_id).", "params": {"deploy": "apred A^B 1/day, hold-60s", "fill_optuna_trials": 25, "reused_models": ["b_universe/A_{SYM}", "b_universe/B_{SYM}_g5", "xgb_maker/B_pool"], "seed": 0}, "repro_cmd": "python3 subs60_xgb_fill.py --symbols BTC LINK --trials 25 ; python3 subs60_xgb_abc.py --symbols BTC LINK", "setup": "Model C = maker-FILL predictor: will a resting limit on side s be HIT within the 12s entry window (target fill_long / fill_short). Two uses tested: (1) standalone predictability + does the fill-asymmetry carry 60s direction; (2) C as a THIRD selection factor on the apred A^B 1/day deploy (score = rank(pA)*rank(|pB-0.5|)*rank(P(fill on B-side)), both signs), vs the maker apred +3.00 baseline. Reuses saved A + B_g5/B_pool; trains only C (Optuna). Scripts subs60_xgb_fill.py, subs60_xgb_abc.py.", "split_method": "honest_val_test", "status": "exploratory", "supersedes": null, "symbols": ["BTC-USDT-PERP", "LINK-USDT-PERP"], "ts": "2026-06-02T18:05:00Z"}
