line -- pooled net -3...-8 bp (e.g. cascade A-5%pool->1/day: net -3.2, gross +2.6). MECHANISM findings (interesting, carry forward): (1) Stage-1 OBJECTIVE drives the config -- predicting the MOVE (regressor on rH) makes grid_sim pick a HIGH-TP/SL c* (BTC RR2.9 then RR6.8 with captured-alpha selection) whereas a binary better-side target picks hold; (2) the high-TP/SL c* chosen on VAL did NOT transfer to TEST on these conditions (val-optimistic, test-worse -- same val->test gap the maker-R:R argmax showed); (3) a true global-correlation IC custom-obj UNDERFITS XGBoost greedy trees (dir-AUC 0.50) -- the regressor is the XGB-native 'predict the move'; (4) taker-B2 raw-60s-direction dir-acc RISES with B-confidence (BTC 0.511->0.542 at top-0.5%) but stayed ~0.54 here -- and crucially the strongly-predictable conviction signal in §15 (dir-acc 0.66-0.77) is the MAKER-better-SIDE (fill microstructure), DISTINCT from raw 60s direction. So 'direction is predictable at selectivity' holds for the maker-fill-favorability (which maker +3.00 exploits at 4bp), not measured-strong here for raw direction needed by taker. NOT a claim that taker/high-TP-SL is impossible -- only that THIS session, on THESE conditions, taker-positive economics beating +3.00 were not achieved. Untested / next: walk-forward c* selection; RR/SL-floor-constrained configs; sequence-model or longer-context direction (GRU got dir-acc 0.612, but those §14 economics carried test=val inflation + mid-entry optimism); lower fee tiers; other horizons. Also recorded: grid_sim --absolute-timeout (exit at t0+60 vs fill+60) -> absolute ~ fill-relative, corr 0.998-0.999 (horizon drift small, fills are fast ~1-5s). All weights+preds+labels persisted (cache_id).", "params": {"cstar_select": "mean net on top-3000 conviction VAL windows", "deploy_budgets_per_day": [1, 2, 5, 10], "gate_pct": 5.0, "grid": "n_tp*n_sl up to ~368 cfgs, RR clip [0.5,30]", "seed": 0, "stage1": "regressor on clipped rH60", "stage2": "executed-payoff 