{"hypothesis_id": "OPS-EXEC", "rev": 1, "ts": "2026-07-26T01:40:00Z", "status": "measured", "experiment_id": "exec_lock_audit-20260726", "summary": "CONFIRMED, colossal. (a) LIVE decision logs 0716-0725 (GCS axb_shadow_h150/*/decisions): DOGE FIXQ t10 gave 104 budget signals / 15 executed = 85.6% dropped by the busy lock (0723: 79 signals -> 6 trades); XRP 3/2, ETH 3/2 (their frozen/dyn taus under-trade live, drops small so far but same lock). (b) Empirical busy from DOGE trade logs: filled trades occupy 152-183s (med 155s; entry fills ~instant, exit chase seconds), entry_miss 60s. (c) Lock-sim on the recorder replay artifacts (_recev_h150anch2_*, 17d 0628-0714, deployed frozen taus): DOGE measured-policy +75.3 bpd / 9.47 tpd / EV +7.95 vs busy-locked +3.1 bpd / 3.24 tpd / EV +0.96 = 4.1% of bpd KEPT; XRP +76.7 bpd -> +17.6 bpd = 22.9% kept. Lock takes the systematically WORST trade of each cluster (DOGE cluster-first EV +2.93 vs cluster-rest +10.27). (d) Slot-sim (M concurrent, one-way skip-opposite; opposite-side overlap DOGE 4.3%/XRP 0%): DOGE kept bpd 4.1/7.9/17.7/30.1/62.8/84.9% at M=1/2/3/4/6/8; XRP 22.9/39.2/53.8/68.6/85.8/98.3%. Full fidelity needs M~8 slots x >=5.5 USDC minNotional-safe per-trade notional = ~44 USDC notional per symbol; current shared balance 20.43 USDC / 4 instances cannot host it (capital decision -> user). Realized live FIXQ-era DOGE: 13 trades EV +10.88bp (n too small to contradict the lock-sim; SE~7bp).", "note": "Scripts scripts/subs60_live_drop_audit.py + subs60_exec_lock_quant.py + subs60_exec_slot_sens.py; fix implemented live/axb_exec.py v3 (slot pool MAX_CONC, same-side stacking, per-trade reduce-only exits by OWN qty, fixed per-trade notional wallet*SIZE_FRAC*MULT/MAX_CONC, skip_opposite; MAX_CONC=1 == legacy bit-for-bit semantics; offline mock test live/test_axb_exec_slots.py 4/4 PASS). NOT deployed: M/capital/leverage choice pending user. Side findings: prod exec files fork 3-way (DOGE=BTC old precision map; ETH +LEVERAGE/NOTI