{"hypothesis_id": "OPS-EXEC", "rev": 2, "ts": "2026-07-26T01:05:00Z", "status": "deployed", "experiment_id": "exec_v3_deploy-20260726", "summary": "USER DECISION executed: (1) DOGE = the ONLY live instance, whole 20.43 USDC deposit, exec v3 slot-pool live 2026-07-26 00:24:57 UTC (md5 48d2da4c92b34de1); config MAX_CONC=8, SIZE_FRAC=1.0, NOTIONAL_MULT=2.2, LEVERAGE=3 (accepted resp=3), DAY_TRADES_HALT=120 -> per-trade ~5.6 USDC, peak 8 slots ~45 notional (2.2x balance), worst simultaneous hard-stop hit ~-1.4 USDC; slot-sim fidelity ~85% of validated bpd. (2) XRP/ETH/BTC OUT OF LIVE, VMs STOPPED ~00:35 UTC (axb-xrp-1/axb-eth-1/axb-btc-1); counterfactual = recorder replay, prefixes _recev_h150anch2_{DOGE_fw0716,XRP_fw0721}/_recev_h150notod_ETH_fw0723 seeded (hd2 started for the replay, STOPPED after). (3) PER-TRADE LIVE-VS-SIM PARITY 0716-0725 (20 events): 16/16 live fills also sim-filled, pnl corr 0.935, med |d| 2.3bp, sim bias +1.7bp; BUT live entry_miss 3/19 attempts vs sim 0 - fills are modeled on the USDT book while execution is on thinner USDC; misses are winner-skewed (sim +53/+35/+8bp; 2/3 matches solid, 1 uncertain dscore .07) -> empirical per-attempt haircut ~x0.6 (n=19, wide CI). Realistic v3 expectation: 85% slot fidelity x 0.6-0.85 fill haircut of the +75 bpd window cell. 1/17 trades had executed-flag socket-race in the decision log (trade real, flag false).", "note": "Showcase updated same window (trading_algorithm main c2e2828: DEPLOYMENTS.md rewrite, exec v3 + unit snapshot, per-trade parity row). Join script scratchpad trade_parity_join.py; monitor rule: weekly per-trade parity from the DOGE anchor, shadow decisions only on pessimized lower bound (run-out mark -> taker cross, stacked-order queue penalty) - pessimized replay variant NOT yet implemented. GCP: budget $6.5 left; running spend now = recorder VM only (~$1.6-2/day incl disks/IPs) -> ~3-4 day runway for the WHOLE system (DOGE engine+exec live on that VM).", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "OPS-EXEC", "rev": 3, "ts": "2026-07-26T02:05:00Z", "status": "measured", "experiment_id": "exec_m8_cell-20260726_fw", "summary": "The DEPLOYED config's own cell, fresh forward window 0715-0724 (10d, recorder replay, frozen tau .817010, USDT-fill layer): UNBOUNDED measured policy 96tr (9.6/d) EV +10.75 bpd +103.2; DEPLOYED M=8 one-way 64tr (6.4/d) EV +9.60 bpd +61.5 (60% of unbounded bpd; 85% on the 0628-0714 window - the M=8 truncation costs more on burst-heavy windows, range 60-85%); old M=1 lock 18tr +11.1 bpd (matches live 15 exec). Deployed deviations from the measured policy, each quantified: (a) slot cap 8 vs observed peak concurrency 15 (DOGE window) - zero-gap needs wallet >= 5.5*M/2.2 ~ $38 for M=15; (b) opposite-side skip = 4.3% of signals; (c) DAY_TRADES_HALT=120 - never bound in observed data (max 79 signals/day). Recorder DOES record USDC pairs since 2026-06-01 (DOGEUSDC depth 1313 hourly files) - the USDT fill layer is a frozen-protocol legacy, not a data constraint.", "note": "NEXT PREREG CANDIDATES (not run): (1) recev-USDC-fills - features/score unchanged (USDT, as live), entry/exit fill sim on the DOGEUSDC book+flow from 06-01 (~55d) - removes the venue fill optimism (3/19 live misses vs sim 0, winner-skewed) from gates and forward counterfactual; parity ritual vs USDT layer required. (2) pegged-entry policy (requote to touch during the 60s window, like the exit chase) to cut entry misses - buys fills at adverse-selection prices, must be measured on the USDC fill layer first. Year-scale USDC = data purchase only.", "priority_rank": 1}
