{"hypothesis_id": "OPS-EXEC", "rev": 5, "ts": "2026-07-26T03:20:00Z", "status": "measured", "experiment_id": "exec_year_concurrency-20260726", "summary": "USER CHALLENGE (why M=15?) CONFIRMED AS MY SCOPE ERROR: 15 was the 17d recorder-window peak, NOT a year property. YEAR walk-forward concurrency profile (FIXQ t10 ens replication from PERFOLD, sanity +10.24/+72.8 vs recorded +10.51/+74.9, 169 test days): daily peak concurrency p50=0 / p90=16 / p99=45 / MAX=50 - FIXQ concentrates the whole year edge into burst-day stacks. Year M-ladder: M=8 keeps 20.7%, M=15 47.4% (+34.5 bpd, EV +6.48), M=20 68.6%, M=31 94.1% (+68.5, EV +10.10), M=50 100% (+72.8, EV +10.24). TRUNCATION WORSENS RISK TOO: worst year day -999.8bp at M=15 vs -674.5bp at M=31/50; daily Sharpe(ann) 3.05 vs 4.88/5.01 - small M drops the best (late-cluster) trades, keeping the worst early ones (same mechanism as the v2 lock). Measured worst day at M=31/50 in equity terms at per-trade 5.5 USDC = -0.37 USDC (-1.8% of 20.43); theoretical all-stops bound: M=31 -25%, M=50 -40% (never approached in the measured year); real residual tail = flash-gap slippage past stops.", "note": "Deployed M=15 therefore keeps only ~47% of the year cell bpd - options at wallet 20.43 (per-trade ~5.9, skip_small floor ~18.1): M=31 MULT=9.0 LEV=15 (peak notional 184 = 9x, margin 60%) or M=50 MULT=14.5 LEV=25 (peak 296 = 14.5x, margin 58%, zero-gap to the year cell). Decision = user risk appetite on the theoretical stop-bound (-25% vs -40%); measured-year risk identical. PERFOLD-derived; rows-in-grid-order assumption same as recev artifacts.", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "OPS-EXEC", "rev": 6, "ts": "2026-07-26T03:55:00Z", "status": "deployed", "experiment_id": "exec_m50_final-20260726", "summary": "USER PICKED M=50 (zero-gap to the year cell). DEPLOYED 2026-07-26 01:41:53 UTC flat-checked: MAX_CONC=50, NOTIONAL_MULT=14.5, LEVERAGE=25 (exchange accepted resp=25), DAY_TRADES_HALT=250 -> per-trade ~5.9 USDC, peak 50 slots ~296 notional (14.5x balance), initial margin ~58%; measured year worst day -2.0% equity, all-stops theoretical bound -43% (user-accepted, test capital), skip_small floor wallet ~18.1. Deploy now trades the FULL measured year policy (FIXQ t10, every above-tau signal, unbounded-equivalent stacking: year peak was exactly 50). Morning sequence M=8 (00:24) -> 15 (00:57) -> 50 (01:41).", "note": "Showcase same-window. Remaining known gaps live-vs-measured: (a) opposite-side skip 4.3% of signals (one-way mode), (b) entry-fill venue optimism ~x0.6/attempt (USDT-book sim fills vs USDC exec) - next levers: USDC fill layer + pegged entry (rev3 note), (c) day halts (250 trades / -5% day-loss) as catastrophic guards only. Watch first burst day: realized stack depth + skip_opposite count + margin behavior vs replay.", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "OPS-EXEC", "rev": 7, "ts": "2026-07-26T04:30:00Z", "status": "measured", "experiment_id": "exec_lock_counterfactual-20260726", "summary": "COST OF THE LOCK, quantified both scales. (A) SAME LIVE WINDOW (FIXQ era 0715-0725, replay 0715-0724, 0725 had 0 signals): ACTUAL live busy-lock 16 trades EV +5.72bp sum +91.6bp = +0.0919 USDC = +0.45% of 20.43 (per-trade notional 10.10). VALIDATED policy on the same days: 96 trades EV +10.75 bpd +103.2 -> at the M=50 per-trade notional 5.92 = +0.612 USDC = +2.99% (6.7x the lock); with the empirical x0.586 venue-fill haircut +0.358 USDC = +1.75% (3.9x). Lock-sim M=1 reproduces the live outcome (+0.112 vs realized +0.0919 USDC) - the counterfactual machinery is anchored. Day structure: the whole window edge is one burst day 0723 (68 trades +980bp = +0.581 USDC) that the lock could only sample 6 times; deployed-policy worst day on the window -0.048 USDC, 2/10 negative days; the one-way skip cost 0 filled trades here (burst was one-sided). (B) YEAR SCALE (169 test days): VALIDATED/deployed M=50 bpd +72.8 = +0.0431 USDC/day = +6.33%/mo at 20.43 equity, daily Sharpe 5.01, worst day -0.400 USDC (-2.0%), 11/169 negative days; with haircut +3.71%/mo; OLD LOCK M=1 bpd +3.9 = +0.0040 USDC/day = +0.59%/mo, Sharpe 1.50, worst day -0.367 (-1.8%) - i.e. the lock kept 5.4% of the year economics while carrying ~the same worst-day loss.", "note": "USDC figures are linear (no compounding), maker 0% fee, funding ignored (150s holds); haircut 0.586 = live/sim total over the 19 sampled live attempts (cluster-first population, wide CI - it may not transfer to the full 96-trade population). 10-day window figures are a window cell, not a rate: the year row is the economics claim.", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "OPS-EXEC", "rev": 8, "ts": "2026-07-26T05:10:00Z", "status": "measured", "experiment_id": "exec_sizing_convention-20260726", "summary": "USER CAUGHT a mismatch between OPS-EXEC rev7 (+6.33%/mo) and showcase README 4.1 (DOGE +12.0%/mo @0.5, +23.6%/mo @100%). SAME CELL, different sizing convention - and the README convention is not deployable. README converts EV/tr x tr/day to ROI assuming per-trade notional = FRAC x equity WITH SEQUENTIAL PER-TRADE COMPOUNDING = a one-position-at-a-time model (the same mental model that produced the busy-lock), while the cell itself peaks at 50 CONCURRENT trades. Binding constraint is gross, not equity: peak_gross = M x per_trade <= lev x equity x margin. @0.5 uncapped = 511 USDC gross = 25x equity = 100% margin at lev 25 (unfundable); @100% = 50x (impossible). NEW MEASURED LADDER at CONSTANT peak gross 296 USDC (lev 25, margin 58%, per_trade = 296/M), year 169d: M=12/15/20/25/31/40/50 -> bpd 28.1/34.5/50.0/62.8/68.5/72.7/72.8, monthly +10.19/+10.01/+10.87/+10.93/+9.61/+7.91/+6.33%, Sharpe 2.39/3.05/4.53/4.98/4.88/5.02/5.01, worst day -15.5/-9.7/-4.8/-4.2/-3.2/-2.4/-2.0%. RETURN PER UNIT OF MARGIN PEAKS AT M=20-25, NOT M=50: sizing for the rare 50-deep stack (p90 daily peak is only 16) starves every normal day. M=25 = 1.7x the return of the deployed M=50 at essentially equal Sharpe (4.98 vs 5.01), deeper worst day (-4.2 vs -2.0%), IDENTICAL catastrophic bound (-43%, set by gross which is held constant).", "note": "Showcase fixed same window (README correction block + new 4.1a deployable ladder; portfolio rows marked historical). NOT changed in production: M stays 50 pending user risk decision (M=25 would be an informed measured deviation, not a silent one). With the x0.59 venue haircut: M=50 -> +3.7%/mo, M=25 -> +6.4%/mo. Caveat: the ladder's truncation model = skip signals while M slots are full (same sim as rev5); Sharpe is scale-invariant so it is convention-free, ROI/worst-day are not.", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "OPS-EXEC", "rev": 9, "ts": "2026-07-26T05:35:00Z", "status": "note", "experiment_id": "exec_objective_correction-20260726", "summary": "USER DIRECTIVE + MY FRAMING ERROR CORRECTED: there is no production and no income - the ~20 USDC live instance is a MEASUREMENT ANCHOR, not a revenue source. rev8's 'return per unit margin peaks at M=20-25, 1.7x more' optimized the wrong objective: at this deposit the difference is ~4 cents/day (0.074 vs 0.043 USDC/day) while the cost is zero-gap fidelity to the measured policy - the property that makes any live-vs-sim divergence attributable to execution instead of confounded by a truncation parameter. M=50 STAYS DEPLOYED. Correct risk formulation for an anchor is LOSS OF THE DATA STREAM, not drawdown-as-loss: below wallet ~17.40 USDC (-14.8% from 20.43) per-trade notional falls under minNotional 5 -> the instance stops trading AND stops emitting parity data. Measured year drawdown at M=50: worst day -1.96%, max DD -2.50% of deposit = ~6x headroom to that floor (at M=25 it would be -4.18%/-5.28%, ~3x). The M~=20-25 capacity optimum is retained as a measured curve for a future capital-scale decision only.", "note": "Showcase 4.1a reframed same window (measurement-anchor framing, data-stop floor, M=25 demoted to capacity observation). Memory: research/memory/live-deposit-is-an-instrument.md (feedback). Selection criterion going forward: information per unit of risk; at equal information prefer the configuration closest to the measured cell.", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "OPS-EXEC", "rev": 10, "ts": "2026-07-26T06:30:00Z", "status": "measured", "experiment_id": "exec_capacity_and_missforensics-20260726", "summary": "TWO USER CHECKS ANSWERED. (1) CONCURRENCY IS NOT CAPITAL-INFEASIBLE - my earlier 'unreachable' framing was wrong. Position mode is ONE-WAY (dualSidePosition=false): same-side entries NET INTO ONE position, so 'M positions' is not an exchange object; constraints are aggregate notional vs margin and per-order >= minNotional 5 USDC (DOGEUSDC: minQty 1 DOGE, tick 1e-5, maxLev 75 up to 10k notional, mmr 0.005; 200 open orders/symbol; 300 orders/10s). Deployed gross 296 USDC = 14.5x wallet: margin 58% at lev 25 (19% at lev 75), liquidation distance 6.40% vs the 3% hard stop. TRUE CEILING is liquidation geometry, not capital: gross <= wallet/(stop+mmr) = 584 USDC keeps a simultaneous all-stop event reachable before liquidation -> M_max ~116 at the 5-USDC floor, vs year peak 50 needed. What IS pinned is per-trade SIZE at the minNotional floor (caps daily PnL, not fidelity) - under the measurement-anchor objective that is the correct thing to be capped. (2) ENTRY-MISS CAUSE IDENTIFIED, user hypothesis PARTIALLY confirmed but not dominant: ZERO entry_reject/EXPIRED events in any log - all 3 misses were entry_placed (orderId issued, order rested) -> 60s -> canceled unfilled, so 'engine rejected on a small price difference' is refuted mechanically. Root cause measured on the recorder DOGEUSDC book: USDT carries ~20x the aggressive-sell flow of USDC (median 20.4x in the same windows); at our price the USDC sell volume was LITERALLY ZERO for all 60s in all three misses, while the USDT-book sim had 0.89-1.96M DOGE hitting the equivalent level -> sim fills, live cannot. Trajectory in all three: we buy a fast dip, price bounces within ~1s and the bid stays ABOVE us 92-100% of the window = the maker paradox (passive fills happen mostly when the signal is wrong; immediately-right trades do not fill) - the mechanism behind the winner-skew. Miss#3 looked like a stale quote (our 0.07138 vs touch 0.07143 = 7bp below at log time) but reconstruction shows the bid genuinely WAS 0.07138 at t0-0.1s: a 30bp dip with instant bounce - not a feed bug, but it exposes the design asymmetry that the ENTRY is fire-and-forget (one price, 60s, no re-quote) while the EXIT chases the touch. HUSDC 'venues differ negligibly' is REFUTED as a level claim: measured USDC-USDT mid basis -2.6 to -7.9bp (persistent, USDC cheaper) with intra-60s sd 0.7-9.3bp against a +10bp/trade edge - it does NOT cause the misses (we quote off the USDC book, basis cancels at placement) but it DOES leak into every sim PnL, which prices both entry and exit on USDT.", "note": "Script scripts/subs60_entry_miss_forensics.py (6 events: 3 misses + 3 fills incl. same-hour control 0723 12:36 miss vs 12:46 fill). Both prereg candidates from rev3 now evidence-backed: (a) USDC fill layer - removes the 20x flow error AND the basis leak, recorder has DOGEUSDC depth+aggTrade since 2026-06-01; (b) pegged/re-quoting entry - would have filled all three, but at post-bounce prices (buys the adverse-selection side), so measure on the USDC layer BEFORE any deploy. Haircut x0.59 stands as an empirical correction with its mechanism now identified.", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "OPS-EXEC", "rev": 11, "ts": "2026-07-26T07:05:00Z", "status": "measured", "experiment_id": "exec_missed_entry_reachability-20260726", "summary": "USER: 'did the price actually not reach our order?' - resolved per event on the DOGEUSDC book, and it REFINES rev10 (whose '92-100% of the window the bid stayed above us' was true but hid the magnitude). miss#1 (BUY 137 @0.07323): price DID reach our exact level for 0.7s of 60 (6/413 snapshots); ZERO trades occurred there - lowest traded price in the whole window was 0.07324 = exactly ONE TICK above us; queue ahead when we became touch 29,730 DOGE (so even arriving flow would have had to clear ~$2.2k before our 137). miss#2 (BUY 140 @0.07146): reached for 1.1s (8/471); zero trades at our price, lowest trade 0.07147 = one tick above; queue ahead only 1,633 DOGE - a mere ~1.8k DOGE of aggressive sells during those 1.1s would have filled us, none came (USDT had 1.96M at the equivalent level). miss#3 (BUY 141 @0.07138): price NEVER reached us - lowest bid in the entire 60s was 0.07139, i.e. we missed by exactly ONE TICK (1.4bp); lowest trade 0.07140. Distance distribution (share of window with best_bid N ticks above our order) shows these were NOT near-misses overall: median gap 14/24/12 ticks (19.1/33.6/16.8bp), with >10 ticks for 71/93/68% of the window - a brief touch, then the price left. PEGGED-ENTRY ARITHMETIC on exactly these three: re-quoting to the median level costs 19.1/33.6/16.8bp against sim PnL +35.48/+53.15/+8.38 -> net +16.4/+19.6/-8.4bp (sum +27.6bp over three trades that today yield 0).", "note": "Script scripts/subs60_did_price_reach.py (classifies A: never reached / B: reached but no flow / C: reached with flow but queue not cleared; miss#1 = B with a deep queue, miss#2 = B with a shallow queue, miss#3 = A). The chase arithmetic is POST-HOC on 3 sim-winning misses and must not be read as the value of a pegged entry: that policy changes behaviour on ALL signals, including currently-missed ones that would LOSE and currently-filled ones that would fill worse. Proper evaluation = full-population USDC fill layer (prereg candidate a) then pegged-entry variant on top (candidate b).", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "OPS-EXEC", "rev": 12, "ts": "2026-07-26T07:45:00Z", "status": "measured", "experiment_id": "exec_sim_fill_branch_attrib-20260726", "summary": "USER: 'doesn't the sim model always-last-in-queue?' / 'or is it exactly the USDT-USDC difference?' - BOTH answered from the simulator source + per-event branch attribution; CORRECTS the rev10/rev11 attribution which credited the misses to flow alone. (A) The queue model IS conservative: production invokes grid_sim_exitdbg with --queue-mult 1.0 (entry queue-ahead = FULL resting depth at our level) and --exit-queue-mult 1.0 (pegged exit = full close-touch depth) = always-last on both legs. Queue position is NOT the source of optimism. (B) BUT simulate_maker_entry (live_sim.rs:752) has a second branch that BYPASSES the queue entirely: 'if b.bid < level_px - eps { return FILLED at level }' - if the best bid drops even one tick below our resting buy, the sim declares a fill with zero flow required and zero queue consumed. Reality splits that case in two: the level was traded through (fill only if flow > queue ahead) OR the level was CANCELLED (we are merely top-of-book, unfilled). The sim collapses both into 'filled'. ALL THREE sim fills came through this branch (t0+1.2s / +3.3s / +0.1s). (C) Venue attribution, per event: miss#1 USDT flow at level 550,807 > queue 485,150 and miss#3 987,518 > 676,123 -> the queue branch would have filled them too, so for 2/3 the FLOW difference is the real driver (USDC had ZERO flow at our level); miss#2 had ZERO flow at the USDT level too and queue 12,000 -> it filled ONLY because of the gap-through shortcut. (D) Placement-level difference measured at t0: USDC bid was -8.2 / -19.6 / -12.6 bp below the USDT bid at the instant of placement - far beyond the -2.6..-7.9bp mean basis, i.e. the engine fires exactly when the books are momentarily desynced and our exec quotes into a USDC-local dip, sitting at the bottom tick of the whole 60s window while the sim's USDT order sits mid-path where any dip trades through it. So the answer to the user is: not the queue model, and yes the USDT-USDC difference - in two separable components, flow (2/3) and placement level + gap-through rule (3/3, sole cause in 1/3).", "note": "Actionable: the USDC fill-layer rebuild (prereg candidate a) fixes flow AND placement level; SEPARATELY the gap-through branch is a venue-independent modelling optimism that should be tightened (require cumulative sells at <= level >= queue ahead, i.e. delete the unconditional return) - that is a frozen-measurement-layer change and needs the parity ritual + prereg amendment, and would re-price every historical cell, so it must NOT be silently patched. Sizing of its effect across the full population is unmeasured (these 3 events are a selected tail).", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "OPS-EXEC", "rev": 13, "ts": "2026-07-26T08:30:00Z", "status": "measured", "experiment_id": "exec_oneway_residual_gap-20260726", "summary": "MEASURED: the deployed exec v3 (M=50, one-way skip-opposite) vs the measured policy on the year cell. Turning the opposite-skip OFF reproduces the RECORDED validation cell EXACTLY - n=1204 trades, EV +10.51bp, bpd +74.9 (DEPLOYMENTS.md carries +10.51 / bpd +74.9 from h1fixedtau-20260712_cl_year) - which independently validates the whole PERFOLD replication chain used in rev5/rev8/rev12. With the skip ON (as deployed): n=1202, EV +10.24, bpd +72.8. So the live deploy now sits 2.8% of bpd away from the measured cell, and the M-truncation contributes ZERO (M=50 = the year peak). MEASURED: only 3 of 1424 above-tau signals (0.2%) are opposite-side skips. INFERRED (weak, n=3): those 3 happened to be large winners, so the 2.8% bpd cost is disproportionate to the 0.2% count and is small-sample noise as much as a real effect - do not treat 2.8% as a stable estimate. The netting itself is an accounting fact, not a limit: Binance keeps ONE aggregate position record per symbol (one-way) = net qty + avg entry price, so N logical trades are our own bookkeeping (exec v3 tracks per-slot filled qty/entry and exits its own quantity reduceOnly); the exchange-side limits are aggregate notional vs margin, minNotional 5/order, 200 open orders/symbol, rate limits.", "note": "Closing the residual 2.8% requires hedge mode (dualSidePosition=true -> separate LONG and SHORT position records so opposite-side signals coexist): exec rework (positionSide + reduceOnly semantics), per-side margin, flat-only switch. NOT RECOMMENDED now - the measured trigger is 3 signals in a year and the objective is measurement fidelity, not PnL. Recorded so the option starts from a measured number if it ever matters. Live realized to date (all 24 closed DOGE trades 0708-0724): +92.5bp, +0.0926 USDC = +0.45% of the 20.43 deposit (+0.93% against the pre-2026-07-11 ~10 USDC denominator); n=24, no statistical content.", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "OPS-EXEC", "rev": 14, "ts": "2026-07-26T09:15:00Z", "status": "measured", "experiment_id": "exec_haircut_retraction-20260726", "summary": "RETRACTION of the x0.59 'venue haircut' as a quantitative correction (user challenge: 'are you sure it exists? what exactly does the exchange take 41% with?'). (1) NOTHING is taken: /fapi/v1/income over 2026-07-15..07-26 shows COMMISSION 0 and FUNDING_FEE 0 across 20 realized rows - the whole account delta is pure realized PnL (+0.206890 USDC = +1.01% of the 20.43 deposit; DOGE +0.091890 / ETH +0.088530 / XRP +0.026470). The '41%' was never a cost, it is the difference between a SIMULATED trade list and a REALIZED one. (2) DECOMPOSITION pooled n=19: shortfall 41.4% = 32.4% trades that never happened (3 unfilled entries) + 9.0% per-trade PnL drift on the 16 that did (median |d| 2.3bp, bias +1.7bp). DOGE-only n=15: 55.6% = 44.1% + 11.6%. (3) THE ESTIMATE DOES NOT SURVIVE ITS OWN SAMPLE: bootstrap 90% CI on the live/sim ratio is [0.15, 0.92] pooled and [-0.39, 0.90] DOGE-only - the data cannot distinguish 'no effect' from 'sim is 2x optimistic'. (4) TWO METHOD ERRORS IN MY OWN NUMBER: (a) I pooled three venues - XRP and ETH had ZERO misses and pulled the pooled ratio up to 0.586 while DOGE alone is 0.444, and DOGE is the venue the number was being applied to; (b) the 3 misses rank 1st, 4th and 10th of 15 by sim PnL - had they been average trades the ratio would be 0.634 instead of 0.444, so the entire winner-skew rests on 3 events. (5) Part of the shortfall is not venue at all: per rev12 all three sim fills came through the unconditional gap-through branch, a modelling optimism that would exist on any venue.", "note": "WHAT STANDS (measured): 3 of 15 DOGE entry attempts did not fill while the sim filled them; the mechanism is measured on the recorder USDC book (zero aggressive sell flow at our price for the full 60s); the sim's gap-through branch bypasses its own queue model; the exchange charges nothing. WHAT DOES NOT STAND: any point estimate of the magnitude, the systematicity of the winner-skew, and the split between venue thinness and simulator error. Direction only: sim PnL is an UPPER BOUND on realized. Correct fix remains the full-population USDC fill layer; until then no numeric haircut may be quoted. Showcase corrected in the same window (DEPLOYMENTS parity row + README 4.1a); prior revs that quote x0.59/x0.6 (rev2, rev10, this session's memory) are superseded by this entry.", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "OPS-EXEC", "rev": 15, "ts": "2026-07-26T10:05:00Z", "status": "measured", "experiment_id": "exec_strict_entry_fill-20260726", "summary": "ATTEMPTED FIX OF THE SIMULATOR'S PHANTOM ENTRY FILLS - MEASURED AND REJECTED. Implemented the strict entry rule (a strict gap past our level zeroes the queue ahead but a fill still requires opposing taker flow in that tick) as grid_sim_exitdbg --strict-entry-fill, OFF by default so every historical cell remains byte-reproducible; Long and Short symmetric; invariant asserted in the reference check (strict never fills where the library misses). Reference-checked on the 6 real live events (3 entry misses + 3 fills) against recorder book+flow on BOTH venues, flow aggregated per book-snapshot interval as build_samples does. RESULT: (a) on DOGEUSDT - the book the simulator actually runs on - ALL THREE phantom fills SURVIVE: the gap tick carries plenty of aggressive sell volume, so the branch merely changes label from 'gap-through' to 'gap+flow'. The fix removes nothing where it matters. (b) on DOGEUSDC it turns a REAL live fill (2026-07-23 12:46, fill#B) into a miss = a false negative. (c) ROOT CAUSE of the residual error, newly identified: FlowL1 is PRICE-AGNOSTIC (total taker volume per tick), so 'flow arrived' cannot be conditioned on 'flow arrived at or through OUR level' - any correct entry model needs price-resolved flow emitted by build_samples. CONCLUSION: the 'just fix the simulator code' path is closed at this level; the correct fix is the same workstream as rebuilding the fill layer on the DOGEUSDC book (price-resolved flow + venue swap), not a one-line branch change. No GCP production run was spent to learn this.", "note": "Code kept off-by-default with the measured verdict in its doc comment (scripts/grid_sim_exitdbg.rs) so the next attempt starts from the result instead of re-deriving it; prereg amendment recorded as hypotheses OPS-EXEC rev2 status=measured_insufficient. Reference checker: scripts/subs60_strict_fill_check.py. MEASURED = the 12 venue x event outcomes above; INFERRED = that price-resolved flow would fix it (not yet demonstrated - it is the next prereg, and it must be validated against the same 6 events plus the full population before any cell is re-priced).", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "OPS-EXEC", "rev": 16, "ts": "2026-07-26T12:30:00Z", "status": "measured", "experiment_id": "exec_price_resolved_fill-20260726", "summary": "FIX IMPLEMENTED, COMPILED AND RUN END-TO-END (supersedes the rejected rev15 half-measure). Root blocker was that flow_paths.npy is PRICE-AGNOSTIC, so the entry model could not ask 'did volume trade THROUGH our level' and fell back on an unconditional gap-through fill. Change: (1) build_samples --emit-level-flow writes an ADDITIVE flow_lvl_paths.npy [ns,h,2] = [taker SELL volume at px <= entry_long, taker BUY volume at px >= entry_short] per forward tick; prices are read in a SEPARATE pass so the frozen aggregation is untouched and a run without the flag is byte-identical. (2) grid_sim_exitdbg --strict-entry-fill (requires --level-flow-paths) replaces the library entry with the textbook queue rule: queue = queue_mult x depth-at-level, each tick queue -= volume traded through our level, fill when queue <= 0, else MISS. No book branches, no gap-through. Both OFF by default. VALIDATION: (a) reference model checked against the six real live events on DOGEUSDC = 6/6 (all three live entry misses miss, all three live fills fill), whereas the frozen model scores 3 phantom fills; (b) cargo build clean, binaries rebuilt; (c) END-TO-END on a full real day (DOGEUSDC 2026-07-23, 2833 samples, same protocol as the deploy cells: entry 60s / hold 150s / chase 300s / qm 1.0): frozen long-fill 0.720 short-fill 0.742 vs strict 0.419 / 0.435 - the frozen model over-fills by ~72% relative, and the surviving fills are WORSE (netl -1.78 -> -3.82bp, nets +1.23 -> +0.24bp), which is the adverse-selection signature: the invented fills were the ones where price ran away in our favour.", "note": "MEASURED = the numbers above (one day, DOGEUSDC, UNCONDITIONAL over all decision points, not tau-selected). NOT MEASURED = the effect on the tau-selected cells, on the USDT book that produced every historical cell, and at year scale - that is the GCP-gated re-measurement and no cell may be re-priced before it runs. Code: scripts/build_samples_husdc.rs + scripts/grid_sim_exitdbg.rs (both overlay files, frozen defaults preserved); reference scripts/subs60_price_resolved_fill_ref.py; end-to-end scripts/subs60_smoke_usdc_fill.py. hd2 started for the compile+smoke and STOPPED again (~25 min). Note the smoke ran on the USDC venue deliberately: it exercises both halves of the correction (right model AND right book) that the deploy needs.", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "OPS-EXEC", "rev": 17, "ts": "2026-07-28T14:00:00Z", "status": "measured", "experiment_id": "usdc_fill_3way-20260728", "summary": "USDC FILL-LAYER 3-WAY DECOMPOSITION MEASURED - AND IT REVERSES MY OWN DIRECTION CLAIM. Frozen-tau symbols (valid cells): DOGE, 27 joined recorder days, 752,296 decisions, deployed tau=0.817010 t10, 262 selected: (a) frozen model / USDT book [what every historical cell used] 248 fills 94.7%, EV +8.83, bpd +81.1; (b) frozen model / USDC book [venue alone] 247 fills 94.3%, EV +10.74, bpd +98.2 = 121% of (a); (c) STRICT price-resolved model / USDC book [honest] 219 fills 83.6%, EV +10.63, bpd +86.2 = 106% of (a). XRP, 22 days, tau=0.925442 t5, 86 selected: (a) 80 fills 93.0% EV +15.41 bpd +56.1; (b) 79 fills 91.9% EV +18.09 bpd +65.0 = 116%; (c) 72 fills 83.7% EV +15.69 bpd +51.4 = 92%. MECHANISM: the fill-rate loss is real and in the predicted direction (DOGE 94.7% -> 83.6% on the selected tail), but it is OFFSET by a higher EV per surviving trade because the USDC book carries a WIDER spread - a maker round trip captures more there. Venue cell (b) isolates that: +16..+21% from the venue alone. Net effect on the deployed cells: DOGE +6%, XRP -8%. So 'simulated PnL is an upper bound on realized' (rev14 and everything I said from rev10 onward) is NOT SUPPORTED on these cells - it was extrapolated from 3 entry misses, which turn out to be unrepresentative of the selected population.", "note": "INVALID IN THIS RUN: BTC and ETH. Their cells use dynamic tau and my aggregator reproduced the documented KNOWN_PITFALLS trap - causal() started with an empty buffer, so day 1 selected ~everything (28,631 of 500,957 for BTC = 1590/day instead of 5/day) and the output is an unconditional average, not a cell. Aggregator patched (day-0 warmup, day 0 excluded from the denominator); BTC/ETH must be re-run before any number from them is quoted. MEASURED = the DOGE/XRP rows above (recorder window 0628-0724, n=262 and n=86 selected, NOT a year cell). NOT MEASURED = year-scale effect, and the deploy-window ROI the user asked for (blocked: score artifacts stop at 0715 for BTC whose deploy is 0716, and at 0724 for the rest - the missing post-deploy days are being scored into research_runs/_recev_dep_{SYM}). Runner scripts/subs60_usdc_fill_layer.py, aggregator scripts/subs60_usdc_fill_agg.py.", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "OPS-EXEC", "rev": 18, "ts": "2026-07-28T18:30:00Z", "status": "measured", "experiment_id": "deploy_window_roi-20260728", "summary": "DEPLOY-WINDOW ROI under the DEPLOYED policy (exec v3 slot pool M=50, one-way) and the HONEST fill model (strict price-resolved, USDC book), per symbol from the day its configuration went live to 2026-07-28. Selection: frozen tau for DOGE/XRP, dynamic tau for BTC/ETH warmed up on the days BEFORE the deploy date (never an empty buffer - the rev17 trap). Per symbol: DOGE 14d 0715-0728, 115 trades, EV +8.86bp, bpd +72.8, peak concurrency 28. XRP 14d, 7 trades, EV +15.15, bpd +7.6, peak 2. BTC 13d, 14 trades, EV -0.23, bpd -0.2, peak 5. ETH 12d, 32 trades, EV +17.94, bpd +47.9, peak 10. SCENARIO A (showcase sizing README 4.1 - DOGE 0.5 / XRP 0.5 / ETH 1.25, no BTC; daily compounding, per-trade sequential compounding is invalid under concurrency): DOGE +5.12% window / +11.29% per 30d, XRP +0.53% / +1.14%, ETH +7.36% / +19.43%, PORTFOLIO +13.44% / +31.02%, worst day -0.15%, peak gross 27.5x equity. SCENARIO B (100% capital per symbol, BTC included): DOGE +10.29% / +23.36%, XRP +1.06% / +2.29%, BTC -0.03% / -0.08%, ETH +5.86% / +15.30%, PORTFOLIO +17.92% / +42.36%, peak gross 45x. Cross-check vs the showcase multi-month cells: DOGE @0.5 +11.29%/mo here vs +12.0%/mo published; portfolio +31.0% vs +35.2% - the published economics survive the honest fill model. Divergences are symbol-specific: XRP collapses (+1.14 vs +8.3 published) because it only produced 7 trades in 14 days - the tau seed runs hot and the symbol under-trades, now visible in money; ETH runs higher (+19.4 vs +12.6); BTC is ~zero even counterfactually.", "note": "BINDING CAVEAT (user directive 2026-07-28): 12-14 days is statistically meaningless next to the multi-month validation cells and these ROI figures MUST NOT be published beside them as 'the real numbers'. What IS publishable is the same-window fill-model comparison (rev17). maxDD ~0 here is an artifact of short mostly-positive windows, not a risk estimate. Peak gross 27.5x/45x is not fundable at the current deposit (liquidation geometry caps ~28x at a 3% stop). Samples: XRP n=7, BTC n=14, ETH n=32 - only DOGE (n=115) carries weight. Live cross-check DOGE same window: sim 115 trades vs ~22 realized (Binance userTrades), the gap being the busy-lock for 11 of the 14 days. Runner scripts/subs60_deploy_roi.py.", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "OPS-EXEC", "rev": 19, "ts": "2026-07-28T18:45:00Z", "status": "note", "experiment_id": "exec_defects_postmortem-20260728", "summary": "POST-MORTEM RECORDED IN THE SHOWCASE as a permanent reminder (user directive). Two production defects, same class - what ran was not what was validated. (1) EXECUTION: the shipped executor held one position at a time while every cell scored every above-tau decision as an independent overlapping trade; 104 signals -> 15 executed (85.6% dropped) on live logs, the lock keeps ~4% of validated bpd and systematically takes the worst trade of each cluster. Cost on the deploy window at showcase sizing: the measured policy returns +13.4% on the 3-symbol portfolio over 14 days while the account realized ~0 - essentially the whole modelled return of the window. Fixed by exec v3 (slot pool) 2026-07-26. (2) SIMULATOR: simulate_maker_entry filled unconditionally on a gap past our level - no flow, no queue - conflating 'traded through' with 'cancelled'. This was an error in building AND validating the simulator; it survived because the queue model around that branch is honest. Fixed opt-in with price-resolved flow, validated 6/6 against live entry outcomes, and the correction turns out to be small (DOGE +6%, XRP -8% on the cells) - i.e. the published edge was roughly right, the execution of it was not.", "note": "Showcase README 4.1a rewritten as this post-mortem plus the legitimate same-window model comparison; engine/src/bin/{build_samples.rs,grid_sim_exitdbg.rs} snapshots updated with the strict model so the validation model itself is preserved in the deploy repo, not only in ml-research. Both flags stay OFF by default: historical artifacts remain byte-reproducible, and a future run gets the broken model unless it passes them (documented in research/runtime/README.md and KNOWN_PITFALLS.md).", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "OPS-EXEC", "rev": 20, "ts": "2026-07-28T20:00:00Z", "status": "measured", "experiment_id": "fill_model_same_window_4sym-20260728", "summary": "SAME-WINDOW FILL-MODEL COMPARISON, ALL FOUR SYMBOLS, deploy windows, dynamic-tau warmed up on pre-deploy days (the rev17 trap is fixed, so BTC/ETH are valid here). Format: trades / EV per trade / bpd, under (a) frozen model on the USDT book = what the published cells use, (b) frozen model on the USDC book = venue alone, (c) STRICT price-resolved model on the USDC book = honest. DOGE 14d: (a) 129 / +8.58 / +79.1, (b) 126 / +8.85 / +79.6, (c) 115 / +8.86 / +72.8 -> 92% of (a). XRP 14d: (a) 8 / +12.43 / +7.1, (b) 8 / +13.37 / +7.6, (c) 7 / +15.15 / +7.6 -> 107%. BTC 13d: (a) 15 / +0.97 / +1.1, (b) 14 / +0.35 / +0.4, (c) 14 / -0.23 / -0.2 -> turns slightly negative on numbers that are ~zero either way. ETH 12d: (a) 31 / +15.84 / +40.9, (b) 30 / +15.95 / +39.9, (c) 32 / +17.94 / +47.9 -> 117%. Read together with rev17 (longer recorder windows: DOGE 106% over 27d, XRP 92% over 22d) the correction is bounded within roughly +/-10-20% and is NOT systematically one-directional: the fill-rate loss (real, predicted) is offset by higher EV per surviving trade on the wider USDC spread. ETH also gains trades under the strict model (31 -> 32), which is possible because the slot pool frees a slot earlier when an entry misses.", "note": "MEASURED = the twelve cells above. Sample sizes are small (XRP 7-8, BTC 14-15, ETH 30-32 trades; only DOGE ~115-129 carries weight) and the windows are 12-14 days, so these are FILL-MODEL comparisons on identical decisions, NOT validation cells and NOT to be quoted beside the multi-month economics (user directive 2026-07-28). Conclusion for the deploy question: the published edge was approximately right; the loss was in execution, not in the fill model. hd2 stopped after the run.", "priority_rank": 1}
{"experiment_id": "modelcap-20260730_v1cap_parity_gate", "hypothesis_id": "MODELCAP", "note": "FOLD_ONLY=k added to the cap trainer to buy this gate at 1/6 of a full job (~27 min under contention vs ~2.2h); folds share no mutable state, which is the same property that made FOLD_PAR parity-safe. Frozen scripts subs60_xgb_optuna_ic.py and subs60_xgb_sobol_v2.py are UNCHANGED - md5 of the v2.1 copy verified as 2a435f32e2517479e0232260c85aad1a, matching the HD3 rev19 prereg. Full capture campaign (DOGE/XRP/BTC 4 seeds via v1cap, ETH 8 seeds via v2cap with DROP_COLS=67-70) launched on hd2, chained behind the OPS-FILLYEAR rebuild.", "priority_rank": 1, "rev": 1, "status": "measured", "summary": "PARITY GATE PASSED BIT-EXACT. subs60_xgb_optuna_ic_v1cap.py (= the frozen v1 trainer + output-only capture of every search-trial booster and the final A/Bg/Bf) was re-run on DOGE x maker_labels_tb3s_h150anch x SEED0 x fold0 (FOLD_ONLY=0, nthread=4->2 under contention, N_TRIALS=25, CFGIDX=1) and reproduces the stored PERFOLD_S0_DOGE_qm0_f0.npz artifact BIT-EXACTLY on all 11 arrays: axb_tr (4,738,312), axb_te / noa_te / day_te / side / side_f / fl / fs / netl / nets (733,418 each), day_tr. Total 5.4M values, zero differences. CONSEQUENCES: (1) the capture patch is proven output-only - it does not perturb the RNG stream, the TPE trajectory or the training path; (2) the boosters it writes ARE the models that produced the published cells, not lookalikes retrained from scratch; (3) the v1 protocol is exactly reproducible on this VM image today (xgboost 3.2.0), which was not previously demonstrated. Artifacts went to research_runs/_modelcap_parity/DOGE_S0/ - the original PERFOLD and OPTUNA_IC artifacts were NOT touched (verified by timestamp: the original OPTUNA_IC_DOGE_qm0.json still dated 2026-07-09). The probe also produced the first trial-level dump in the program: 25 A-study + 25 B-study boosters + the two index jsons for that fold.", "ts": "2026-07-30T20:40:00Z"}
{"experiment_id": "fillyear-20260730_strict_entry_fill_DOGE_XRP", "hypothesis_id": "OPS-FILLYEAR", "note": "Cells research_runs/strictfill_cells/{DOGE_fixq_t10,XRP_fixq_t5}.json; labels research_runs/maker_labels_tb3s_h150strict/{DOGE,XRP}.npz (frozen AND strict labels stored side by side). Build spec per symbol was MEASURED, not assumed: DOGE H_TICKS=1500 (the DOGE-dedicated builder), XRP 1800 - the first smoke ran DOGE at the cross-symbol 1800 and the ts gate caught it. A worker-directory race in the first runner pass cost 2 DOGE days; both gates flagged them, the combine refused to run, they were re-run after the fix. NOT YET MEASURED in this record: BTC, ETH, and the 4.1 economics columns (monthly ROI / Sharpe / maxDD / correlations) - separate record.", "priority_rank": 1, "rev": 1, "status": "measured", "summary": "PARTIAL RESULT (DOGE and XRP; BTC/ETH still rebuilding). YEAR-SCALE STRICT ENTRY-FILL RE-ACCOUNTING ON THE USDT BOOK - the same models, scores, tau and selection as the published cells, only the fill/PnL labels recomputed with the strict price-resolved queue rule. VALIDATION FIRST: the frozen column, computed through the identical code path, reproduces the published cells EXACTLY - DOGE FIXQ t10 EV +10.513bp n=1204 tpd 7.12 bpd +74.90 (published +10.51 / 1204 / 74.900), XRP FIXQ t5 EV +21.314 n=401 bpd +52.44 (published +21.3143 / 401 / 52.4358). All three row-join gates passed on every fold, and the per-day rebuild reproduced the stored labels bit-exactly on 371/371 DOGE and 365/365 days. STRICT RESULT: DOGE 1424 selected, fills 1204 (84.6%) -> 1198 (84.1%), EV +10.51 -> +11.16, bpd +74.90 -> +79.14 = 106% of the published cell. XRP 446 selected, fills 401 (89.9%) -> 400 (89.7%), EV +21.31 -> +22.80, bpd +52.44 -> +55.96 = 107%. MECHANISM (measured, not inferred): the strict model DOES cut fills hard unconditionally - whole-day fill rate DOGE 0.85 -> 0.59, XRP 0.58 -> 0.16, and the average unconditional trade gets worse (DOGE 2026-05-01 netl150 +1.09 -> -0.26bp), reproducing the rev16 day-level finding - but on the tau-selected tail the fill rate moves by 0.5 and 0.2 percentage points only. The phantom fills lived OUTSIDE the traded tail: the policy selects moments where the level genuinely trades through. CONSEQUENCE FOR THE PROGRAM: the standing warning that 'every maker cell before 2026-07-26 is an upper bound' is NOT supported at year scale for these two deployed cells - the correction is +6% and +7%, in the same bounded, non-one-directional band rev17/rev20 measured on USDC, but here with the venue held fixed so it is the model error alone.", "ts": "2026-07-30T20:45:00Z"}
{"experiment_id": "fillyear-20260730_strict_entry_fill_year_4sym", "hypothesis_id": "OPS-FILLYEAR", "note": "Cells research_runs/strictfill_cells/{DOGE_fixq_t10,XRP_fixq_t5,BTC_dyn_t5,ETH_dyn_t5_growth,ETH_dyn_t5_safety_recon}.json + ECONOMICS_strictfill{,_safety}.json. Labels maker_labels_tb3s_h150strict/{DOGE,XRP}.npz and maker_labels_tb3s_h150dstrict/{BTC,ETH}.npz, frozen and strict labels stored side by side. REBUILD PARITY: 1464 days across 4 symbols, ZERO parity failures - every day's frozen rebuild reproduced the stored pnl/fill bit-exactly and the rebuilt ts matched row-for-row; row counts match the independently recorded rev10 figures (BTC 10,438,107/370d, ETH 10,224,311/361d). H_TICKS measured per symbol (DOGE 1500, XRP 1800, BTC/ETH 5100) - assuming the cross-symbol 1800 for DOGE was caught by the ts gate. ETH SAFETY is a RECONSTRUCTION: the producing script exists on no surviving host, the rule was transcribed from axb_engine.rs v4 (cons = seeds clearing their own frozen tau; block when 2<=cons<=N-2) with the fold-frozen per-seed FIXQ tau its own comment prescribes; it lands at n=295 vs the published 299 but reproduces the published ETH and PORTFOLIO ROI/DD/worst-day rows to the decimal. Invocations: hd2-feats-003 (n2-highmem-8, europe-west1-b) run_strict_all.sh -> cells_dx.sh / cells_be.sh / eth_safety.sh / econ_safety.sh; runners research/runtime/strictfill_{year,cells,economics}.py. NOT MEASURED HERE: cell A2 (retraining on the strict labels) - separate record.", "priority_rank": 1, "rev": 1, "status": "measured", "summary": "CELL A1 COMPLETE - YEAR-SCALE STRICT ENTRY-FILL RE-ACCOUNTING, 4 SYMBOLS, USDT BOOK, SAME MODELS/SCORES/TAU. VALIDATION (the frozen column, same code path): every published 4.1 number reproduced - DOGE +10.51bp n=1204 bpd +74.90 mo +11.97% Sharpe 4.86 DD -17.25% (published +10.51/1204/74.90/+12.0%/4.86/-17.3%); XRP +21.31 n=401 bpd +52.44 mo +8.26% Sh 3.39 DD -8.27%; BTC +12.27 n=449 bpd +32.79 mo +5.09% Sh 2.12 DD -10.90%; ETH growth +15.79 n=430 bpd +42.70 @0.5 mo +6.67% Sh 2.59 DD -8.26%; ETH safety(reconstruction) +17.06 n=295 @1.25 mo +12.64% Sh 2.58 DD -12.12% worst -9.38% (published +16.84/299/+12.6%/2.62/-12.1%/-9.4%); PORTFOLIO DOGE.5+XRP.5+ETHsafety1.25 mo +35.20% Sh 5.20 DD -14.47% worst -9.38% (published +35.2%/5.26/-14.5%/-9.4%); portfolio 4x0.5 mo +32.86% DD -24.78% worst -3.85% (published +32.9%/-24.8%/-3.9%). STRICT RESULT (identical decisions, only the fill model changes): DOGE bpd +74.90->+79.14 = 106%, EV +10.51->+11.16, fills on the selected tail 1204->1198 of 1424 (84.6%->84.1%); XRP +52.44->+55.96 = 107%, EV +21.31->+22.80, 401->400 of 446 (89.9%->89.7%); BTC +32.79->+34.67 = 106%, EV +12.27->+13.12, 449->444 of 468 (95.9%->94.9%); ETH growth +42.70->+45.96 = 108%, EV +15.79->+16.99, 430->430 of 442 (97.3%->97.3%); ETH safety +31.66->+33.57 = 106%, EV +17.06->+17.97, 295->297 of 305 (the strict model GAINS two trades there). Deployed-sizing monthly ROI: DOGE +11.97->+12.69%, XRP +8.26->+8.84%, BTC +5.09->+5.39%, ETH safety +12.64->+13.44%, portfolio +35.20->+37.70% with maxDD -14.47->-14.23% and worst day -9.38->-8.09%. MECHANISM, MEASURED: unconditionally the strict model does cut fills hard - whole-year day-mean fill rate DOGE 0.809->0.672, XRP 0.800->0.658, BTC 0.759->0.617, ETH 0.850->0.741, and the unconditional filled trade gets 0.6-1.1bp WORSE on every symbol, reproducing the rev16 day-level finding - but on the tau-selected tail the fill rate moves by 0.2-1.0 percentage points and the surviving trades are BETTER. The phantom fills were concentrated OUTSIDE the traded tail: the policy selects moments where the level genuinely trades through, which is why the correction is +6..+8% rather than a haircut. CONSEQUENCE: the standing warning that every maker cell before 2026-07-26 is an UPPER BOUND is NOT supported at year scale for the four deployed cells - on the USDT book, with the venue held fixed, the honest fill model raises all five cells by 6-8%.", "ts": "2026-07-30T23:30:00Z"}
{"experiment_id": "modelcap-20260731_full_job_parity_both_protocols", "hypothesis_id": "MODELCAP", "note": "Campaign research_runs/modelcap_{h150anch,h150d,v2notod}/ on xsym-32, 7 concurrent jobs x nthread=4 (~1.6h per job, 14GB RSS each; 90 of 235GB, load 27 of 30). Trial-level dumps land alongside: 25 A-study + 25 B-study boosters per fold plus the index jsons. The frozen trainers subs60_xgb_optuna_ic.py and subs60_xgb_sobol_v2.py are untouched and keep their md5s; the capture lives in the *_v1cap / *_v2cap copies.", "priority_rank": 1, "rev": 1, "status": "measured", "summary": "CAPTURE PARITY SETTLED ON BOTH PROTOCOLS AND ACROSS HOSTS - the recovered boosters are the deployed models, not lookalikes. (1) v1cap, FULL 6-fold jobs, run on xsym-32 (gen-lang-client, 30 vCPU, nthread=4) against artifacts produced in July on a different host at a different thread count: DOGE S0 and XRP S0, 12 of 12 folds BITEXACT on all 11 PERFOLD arrays. So the v1 protocol is deterministic across host, project, vCPU count and thread count - a property that was assumed but never demonstrated. (2) v1cap single-fold probe on hd2: bit-exact (earlier record). (3) v2cap on ETH v2notod S0, which is the stronger check because that cell already had booster dumps: PERFOLD bit-exact 6/6; boosters A and Bg byte-IDENTICAL on all 6 folds; Bf byte-differs on folds 3 and 5 ONLY - investigated to the field level and the sole difference is `sum_hessian`, the cover diagnostic, in 1 of 37,694 values (fold3) and 2 of 31,376 (fold5), max relative 1.2e-7. Split features, split thresholds and leaf weights are identical everywhere, which is exactly why the predictions and therefore PERFOLD come out bit-exact. That residual is float32 summation order across threads, not a model difference. CONCLUSION: parity holds on everything that determines behaviour; an md5 comparison is STRICTER than the property being claimed and will flag this cover statistic - compare boosters field-wise, not by hash.", "ts": "2026-07-31T01:20:00Z"}
{"experiment_id": "modelcap-20260731_ensemble_and_model_anatomy", "hypothesis_id": "MODELCAP", "note": "Runners research/runtime/{ensemble_anatomy,model_anatomy}.py; artifacts research_runs/strictfill_cells/{ANATOMY_{DOGE,XRP,BTC,ETH},MODEL_ANATOMY_{DOGE,XRP,BTC},MODEL_ANATOMY_ALL}.json (360 models, 240 search landscapes). k-seed curves: DOGE 5.61/8.01/9.70/10.51 monotone and NOT saturated at the deployed 4; XRP 14.03/15.49/19.27/21.31 likewise; BTC 9.95/13.29/13.59/12.27 peaks at k=3; ETH (8 seeds) 10.14/13.79/13.48/13.41/14.17/14.57/14.36/15.79. INTERPRETATION LIMIT: all of this is measured on the frozen-label cells over the walk-forward test year; picking a seed subset on these numbers would be test-set selection and is NOT proposed as a deploy change. The BTC observation is recorded as a property of the cell, i.e. its 4 seeds were inherited rather than chosen.", "priority_rank": 1, "rev": 1, "status": "measured", "summary": "WHY THE SEED-ENSEMBLE BEATS ONE SEED, AND WHY SEEDS DIFFER - MEASURED ON THE POPULATION THAT PRODUCED THE PUBLISHED CELLS (20 jobs, 436 final boosters + 5795 trial boosters captured, ~15GiB). (1) SEEDS DO NOT LEARN DIFFERENT STRUCTURE: cross-seed feature-importance agreement (Spearman over the gain ranking) is 0.963-0.991 on every symbol and every model (DOGE A .990 / Bg .985 / Bf .980; XRP .991/.991/.969; BTC .990/.979/.963; ETH .989/.988/.979). (2) THE SEARCH SURFACE IS NEARLY FLAT, so the HP choice is noise: across 24 fold-searches the best-minus-median trial gap is 0.0016 AUC on a mean best of 0.8354 (A) and 0.0023 IC on 0.0367 (B); trial sd 0.0025 / 0.0049; the argmax lands on effectively random trial indices. Within one fold the seeds pick max_depth 3..7 and num_boost_round 53..393 for B - structurally very different models - while their validation metrics agree to the third decimal (fold0 aucA 0.834/0.833/0.833/0.834). (3) THE DIVERGENCE LIVES ENTIRELY IN THE EXTREME TAIL: the policy trades the top 0.04% of decisions (t10 = 10 trades of ~24,800 daily), so score differences invisible in AUC/IC reshuffle the traded set - score rank correlation across seeds 0.52-0.70 but Jaccard of the SELECTED sets only 0.23-0.33, and a single seed would take just 50-65% of the ensemble's decisions. (4) THE ENSEMBLE GAIN IS A RANKING EFFECT, NOT A DIRECTION EFFECT: substituting the ensemble score while keeping one seed's side recovers the entire gain (DOGE +4.90 of +4.90; XRP +7.28 of +7.28; ETH +5.64 of +5.64; BTC +2.20 of +2.32) because on selected rows the seeds already agree on side ~100% of the time (a high AxB score requires a confident |pB-0.5| by construction). (5) TWO RESULTS THAT BREAK 'more seeds is better': cross-seed score DISPERSION does not predict trade quality (corr -0.056 / -0.009 / -0.005 / +0.111), so the ensemble is not avoiding a bad region, it is denoising the ranking; and on BTC a seed's standalone EV does not predict its ensemble contribution - the best 3-seed subset (0,2,3) EV +15.51 INCLUDES the weakest seed (standalone +1.10) and excludes seed1 (standalone +9.74), while 'drop the weakest seed' (1,2,3) is the WORST 3-subset at +12.83; the deployed 4-seed form (+12.27, bpd +32.79) is beaten by three of the four 3-subsets. (6) SYMBOLS DIFFER WHERE SEEDS DO NOT: cross-symbol importance agreement is 0.727-0.958 and clusters as {BTC,ETH} (Bg rho .958) and {DOGE,XRP} (.929) with .741-.833 across the groups - the split that matches book density / H_TICKS and funding semantics. The difference is carried by the DIRECTION model only: the volatility model A is nearly symbol-invariant (feature x38 alone is 45.0-45.6% of gain on all four symbols), while Bg is symbol-specific - DOGE/XRP clock-dominated (~26% of gain in the four time-of-day features), BTC led by x13 (the live funding column, matching the rev19 finding), ETH led by x43 at 19.6% with NO time-of-day feature in its top 8, which independently confirms its no-ToD ablation was applied.", "ts": "2026-07-31T03:30:00Z"}
{"experiment_id": "fillyear-20260731_untraded_population_value", "hypothesis_id": "OPS-FILLYEAR", "note": "Script /tmp/unsel.py pattern (kept in the session log); reuses the same PERFOLD scores and strictfill labels as the A1 cells, so the traded-side numbers reproduce the A1 cells exactly (DOGE +10.513/1204, XRP +21.314/401, BTC +12.268/449, ETH +15.788/430) - which is also a consistency check on this measurement.", "priority_rank": 1, "rev": 1, "status": "measured", "summary": "WHAT THE UNTRADED POPULATION IS WORTH (user challenge: 'why report non-selected statistics at all, and why call the traded set a tail when it IS the whole strategy'). Measured on the same test year, scoring EVERY decision with the ensemble's own side and the frozen labels: DOGE all-filled EV -1.824bp hit 42.96% (3,393,760 filled of 4,191,122 decisions), of which never-traded -1.828bp hit 42.95% (3,392,556) vs traded +10.513bp hit 62.96% (1204 = 0.035% of filled); XRP -1.831/42.80% vs traded +21.314/66.33% (401 = 0.012%); BTC -1.670/42.26% vs +12.268/68.82% (449 = 0.012%); ETH -1.652/43.67% vs +15.788/66.51% (430 = 0.011%). TWO CONSEQUENCES. (1) The untraded population is NOT a coin flip - it is systematically negative at 42-44% hit, the ordinary adverse-selection signature of an unfiltered maker round trip. The strategy trades one decision in ~3,000 (DOGE) to one in ~8,500 (ETH). (2) The unconditional fill-rate figures quoted throughout this program (year day-mean 0.76-0.85 -> 0.62-0.74 under the strict model, unconditional trade 0.6-1.1bp worse) describe exactly that negative population and are a DIAGNOSTIC ONLY - they explain why the fill-model error never reaches the cells, and must not be presented beside cell economics as if they said something about the strategy. Reporting corrected in trading_algorithm README 4.1b and in the entry-fill-model-fix memory; the word 'tail' is dropped for the traded set, which is the entire product rather than a marginal subset. NOT IGNORABLE, HOWEVER: those ~3.4M untraded labels are what the models are TRAINED on - the direction model is fitted on every filled row, the volatility model on every row - so a wrong fill model there corrupts the models even though it does not corrupt the accounting. That is precisely cell A2, running.", "ts": "2026-07-31T04:00:00Z"}
{"experiment_id": "modelcap-20260731_logit_level_decorrelation", "hypothesis_id": "MODELCAP", "note": "Runner research/runtime/logit_anatomy.py; artifacts research_runs/strictfill_cells/LOGIT_ANATOMY_{DOGE,XRP,BTC,ETH}.json. TESTABLE FOLLOW-UP suggested by the pA result, not run: if the per-seed A models agree at 0.97-0.99, an ensemble that keeps ONE A and averages only Bg may be indistinguishable from the deployed N-seed form while nearly halving the engine's scoring cost. That is cheap to test offline on the captured weights and is NOT proposed as a deploy change.", "priority_rank": 1, "rev": 1, "status": "measured", "summary": "WHERE THE CROSS-SEED DECORRELATION LIVES (user question: are the seeds decorrelated enough for the ensemble to work, and is it hiding in the raw A/B logits rather than the composite?). Answered by scoring the captured boosters directly - dataset reloaded and the vol-norm rebuilt exactly as the trainer does, 200k test rows per fold. Cross-seed Spearman, off-diagonal mean: pA 0.991/0.986/0.971/0.994 (DOGE/XRP/BTC/ETH) - the volatility models are near-identical across seeds; pBg 0.654/0.800/0.676/0.701; |pBg-0.5| 0.351/0.535/0.412/0.461 - the quantity the composite actually consumes is the LEAST agreed on every symbol; composite 0.639/0.703/0.526/0.672. SWAP DECOMPOSITION, the decisive test: rebuilding the composite with A varying and Bg pinned to seed0 gives 0.992/0.990/0.987/0.995 - i.e. varying A alone produces essentially NO disagreement - while varying Bg alone gives 0.644/0.711/0.541/0.676, reproducing the full composite disagreement to within 0.005-0.015 on all four symbols. So 100% of the ensemble-relevant decorrelation is carried by the DIRECTION model's confidence magnitude. Raw-probability and rank correlations are nearly equal (pA 0.994 vs 0.991, pBg 0.658 vs 0.654 on DOGE), so this is genuine rank disagreement, NOT a logit-scale/calibration artifact that the per-seed rank-CDF would have normalised away. Note also that |pBg-0.5| is far less agreed than pBg itself (0.351 vs 0.654 on DOGE): the seeds agree on the SIGN of the direction (side agreement ~100% on selected rows) but disagree on the distance from 0.5, which is exactly what the score ranks on. COROLLARY: across these four symbols the size of the ensemble gain is NOT increasing in decorrelation - BTC is the most decorrelated (composite 0.526) and gains least (+2.32bp), XRP the most agreed (0.703) and gains most (+7.28bp). Consistent with averaging only helping when the disagreement is zero-mean: BTC's seeds differ in QUALITY (per-seed EV 1.1/9.7/15.0/13.9, sd 6.32) rather than only in ranking noise, which is also where the k-seed curve is non-monotone (peak at k=3) and subset composition matters. n=4 symbols - stated as a consistent pattern, not a law.", "ts": "2026-07-31T05:10:00Z"}
{"experiment_id": "modelcap-20260731_objective_operating_point_gap", "hypothesis_id": "MODELCAP", "note": "Runner /tmp/ic_gap.py pattern (reuses research/runtime/logit_anatomy.py's vol-norm rebuild). This is an OBSERVATION plus a hypothesis, not a proposal: a tail-weighted or selection-aware B objective is a candidate for its own preregistered tier, and the frozen v1/v2 protocols are not to be edited on the strength of one measurement. Two symbols measured (DOGE fixq t10, BTC dyn t5); XRP/ETH not run.", "priority_rank": 1, "rev": 1, "status": "measured", "summary": "THE TRAINING OBJECTIVE IS MEASURED ON A POPULATION THE POLICY NEVER TRADES (user question: 'is the IC computed over all the noise the models emit, or over the selected decisions?'). FROM THE FROZEN CODE: the B-study objective is corr(pB-0.5, netl-nets) over vb = val & both, i.e. EVERY row of the last 30 training days where both sides would have filled - no tau, no budget, no selection; the A-study objective is AUC over all rows of the same window. MEASURED CONTRAST on the test year with the captured 4-seed mean Bg: DOGE IC over all both-filled test rows +0.0213 (n=2,309,036) vs IC over the tau-selected decisions +0.1625 (n=1,085); BTC +0.0275 (n=2,714,264) vs +0.2063 (n=416). The direction model is ~7.5x more informative at the operating point than on the population its hyperparameters were chosen by. CAVEAT, stated because the comparison is not apples-to-apples: selection partly conditions on large |pB-0.5|, which mechanically concentrates high-|x| points and can inflate a correlation, so the ratio measures the gap between the selection metric and the operating point, not model skill. WHY THIS MATTERS: it is a single mechanism that accounts for three separately measured facts - (a) the search surface is nearly flat (best-minus-median trial 0.0023 IC) because it is scored on the bulk where differences are tiny; (b) the seeds agree everywhere except the traded tail (feature importance 0.98, pA 0.99, side ~100% on selected, but |pBg-0.5| only 0.35-0.54) because nothing in the objective pressures agreement there; (c) a seed's standalone EV does not predict its ensemble contribution. Nothing in the frozen protocol optimises the region that produces the entire P&L.", "ts": "2026-07-31T05:40:00Z"}
{"experiment_id": "fillyear-20260731_cell_A2_strict_label_training_DOGE_XRP", "hypothesis_id": "OPS-FILLYEAR", "note": "Cells research_runs/strictfill_cells/A2_{DOGE_fixq_t10,XRP_fixq_t5,DOGE_dyn_t10,XRP_dyn_t5}.json plus the A1 DYN controls A1_{DOGE,XRP}_dyn_*. Training a2_h150anch_strict on xsym-32, datasets maker_labels_tb3s_h150anch_strict (published features x strict labels, row alignment asserted). FRAMING per CLAUDE.md: this is a conditional characterisation - the condition 'train on honest fills' yields LESS alpha for this architecture - and is NOT a deploy gate and NOT a correction to A1; A1 remains the answer to 'what were the published cells worth under an honest fill model'. Internal consistency check passed on the way: the A1 DYN cells give strict/frozen 105% and 107%, matching the A1 FIXQ 106%/107%. BTC and ETH pending.", "priority_rank": 1, "rev": 1, "status": "measured", "summary": "CELL A2, PARTIAL (DOGE, XRP; BTC/ETH still training). The protocol retrained end-to-end on the STRICT labels - same frozen search, same walk-forward, same 4 seeds, only the fill/PnL labels honest - and evaluated on the strict labels. THE SURFACE: training on honest fills LOWERS the traded cell substantially, on both symbols and under BOTH selection policies. Deployed FIXQ: DOGE A2 EV +4.42 n=1151 bpd +30.11 vs A1 (published models, strict accounting) +11.16 / 1198 / +79.14 = 38%; XRP A2 +5.16 / 760 / +24.06 vs A1 +22.80 / 400 / +55.96 = 43%. Under DYN, which self-calibrates tau daily and therefore controls for threshold drift: DOGE A2 +2.25 / 1167 / +15.53 vs A1 +8.86 / 1230 / +64.47 = 24%; XRP A2 +5.98 / 617 / +22.62 vs A1 +13.56 / 503 / +41.85 = 54%. CONTROL THAT MATTERS: under FIXQ the A2 models over-selected (XRP 849 vs 446 selected), which looked like a threshold artifact - the frozen tau comes from the training-window score distribution. DYN removes that (trade counts converge to 1167 vs 1230 and 617 vs 503) and the deficit REMAINS, so this is a ranking-quality effect at the operating point, not a calibration effect. Hit rate falls with it (DOGE 63.2% -> 56.0% FIXQ, 60.3% -> 53.9% DYN). CONNECTION TO THE OBJECTIVE MEASUREMENT: A2's validation B-IC ROSE about 3x (fold-wise 0.027-0.051 -> 0.083-0.108) while its traded EV FELL 2-4x - the search metric and the outcome moved in OPPOSITE directions, which is the strongest evidence yet that the bulk IC objective (measured over ~2.3M both-filled rows) does not govern the tau-selected 0.04% that produces the P&L. The A-model side is unchanged as expected: its target |rH| >= threshold does not depend on fills, and the per-fold A-AUCs are identical between A1 and A2 (0.858/0.870/0.836/0.808/0.807), which also confirms only the intended labels moved. PLAUSIBLE MECHANISM, NOT MEASURED: the strict rule removes ~1/3 of fills non-randomly - exactly the cases where flow failed to clear the queue - so it changes the noise STRUCTURE of the B target, not just the sample size.", "ts": "2026-07-31T07:30:00Z"}
{"experiment_id": "fillyear-20260731_cell_A2_complete_4sym", "hypothesis_id": "OPS-FILLYEAR", "note": "ARTIFACT MANIFEST (gs://market-data-0998ac51/research_runs/). Strict labels: maker_labels_tb3s_h150strict/{DOGE,XRP}.npz (962MiB) + maker_labels_tb3s_h150dstrict/{BTC,ETH}.npz (1.23GiB), each carrying frozen AND strict labels side by side, plus daily/ and RUNLOG_*.json. A2 datasets (published features x strict labels): maker_labels_tb3s_h150anch_strict (3.48GiB), _h150d_strict (2.08GiB), _h150danch_strict (2.15GiB). MODEL CAPTURE, A1 side: modelcap_h150anch (DOGE+XRP, 192 MODELS / 48 PERFOLD / 2496 TRIALS, 4.16GiB), modelcap_h150d (BTC, 96/24/1248, 2.52GiB), modelcap_v2notod (ETH 8 seeds, 192/48/2496, 5.95GiB). A2 side: a2_h150anch_strict (192/48/2496, 4.13GiB), a2_h150d_strict (96/24/1248, 2.12GiB), a2_v2notod_strict (192/48/2496, 6.00GiB). Every fold carries 52 trial files = 25 A-study boosters + 25 B-study boosters + 2 index jsons with params and objective per trial; ~34GiB captured in total. CELLS AND ANALYSES: strictfill_cells/{DOGE_fixq_t10,XRP_fixq_t5,BTC_dyn_t5,ETH_dyn_t5_growth,ETH_dyn_t5_safety_recon}.json (A1), A2_{DOGE_fixq_t10,DOGE_dyn_t10,XRP_fixq_t5,XRP_dyn_t5,BTC_dyn_t5,ETH_dyn_t5}.json, A1_{DOGE,XRP}_dyn_*.json, ECONOMICS_strictfill{,_safety}.json, ANATOMY_{4 syms}.json, MODEL_ANATOMY_{DOGE,XRP,BTC,ALL}.json, LOGIT_ANATOMY_{4 syms}.json. RUNNERS (committed): research/runtime/strictfill_{year,cells,economics,dataset}.py, {ensemble,model,logit}_anatomy.py, economics_{v1,3sym}.py; trainers scripts/subs60_xgb_{optuna_ic_v1cap,sobol_v2cap}.py (the frozen originals untouched). HOSTS: hd2-feats-003 (labels, cells, analyses) and xsym-32 (both training campaigns, 7 jobs x nthread=4). INTERPRETATION OF THE A2 NUMBERS IS DELIBERATELY NOT IN THIS RECORD (user directive 2026-07-31: record results and artifacts, defer conclusions).", "priority_rank": 1, "rev": 1, "status": "measured", "summary": "CELL A2 COMPLETE, 4 SYMBOLS - RESULTS RECORDED, INTERPRETATION DEFERRED BY USER REQUEST. Protocol retrained end-to-end on the STRICT labels (same frozen search, same walk-forward W200/T30/EMB2, same seed counts, only the fill/PnL labels honest), evaluated on the strict labels; all row-join gates passed on every fold of every symbol. A2 CELLS (deployed policy, ENSEMBLE, strict labels): DOGE FIXQ t10 EV +4.420bp n=1151 tpd 6.81 bpd +30.11 hit 56.0%; XRP FIXQ t5 EV +5.161 n=760 tpd 4.66 bpd +24.06 hit 52.2%; BTC DYN t5 EV +8.778 n=562 tpd 3.35 bpd +29.36 hit 57.3%; ETH DYN t5 (growth form, 8 seeds) EV +6.635 n=375 tpd 2.36 bpd +15.65 hit 58.4%. A2 UNDER DYN FOR THE FIXQ SYMBOLS (policy-matched comparison): DOGE +2.250 / 1167 / +15.53 hit 53.9%; XRP +5.975 / 617 / +22.62 hit 53.6%. A1 DYN CONTROLS RUN IN THE SAME PASS (published models, strict labels): DOGE +8.859 / 1230 / +64.47 hit 60.3% (strict/frozen 105%); XRP +13.561 / 503 / +41.85 hit 59.8% (107%) - consistent with the A1 FIXQ figures 106%/107%. PER-SEED (A2, strict): DOGE 2.815/4.579/4.822/4.058; XRP 10.805/4.088/2.629/2.812; BTC 7.694/10.318/10.480/7.727 (sd 1.55, against A1 BTC per-seed 1.1/9.74/15.01/13.93 sd 6.32). TRAINING DIAGNOSTICS: A-model per-fold AUC identical between A1 and A2 (0.858/0.870/0.836/0.808/0.807 on DOGE S1), as expected since its target |rH|>=thr does not depend on fills; B-study validation IC rose fold-wise from 0.0265-0.0512 to 0.0830-0.1078 on the same seed.", "ts": "2026-07-31T09:15:00Z"}
{"experiment_id": "modelcap-20260801_score_ev_surface_4sym", "hypothesis_id": "MODELCAP", "note": "Runner research/runtime/score_ev_curve.py (committed; docstring carries the exact gcloud fetch). Artifacts research_runs/strictfill_cells/SCORE_EV_CURVES.json (curve data: marginal bands, both cumulative frames, at-deployed-q rows, bulk stats) and SCORE_EV_CURVES.html (the rendered four-panel figure). Inputs: 120 PERFOLD artifacts, 3.2GiB, score_subs as each cell records them - DOGE/XRP maker_labels_tb3s_h150anch (4 seeds), BTC maker_labels_tb3s_h150d (4 seeds), ETH maker_labels_tb3s_h150danch_v2notod (8 seeds); 6 folds each. Run on the Windows workstation, ~4 min CPU, no VM. Accounting identical to strictfill_cells.py; FROZEN labels only - the strict (cell A2) label set was NOT included and the same curve under honest fills is not measured here. SCOPE LIMITS, stated because the shape invites over-reading: the cumulative curve at the far-left of the traded region rests on 50-350 trades, so its LEVEL is noisy even though its slope is not; ETH is the growth form (no HARMONY); the marginal bands are pooled over folds after within-fold ranking, so a band mixes regimes; and this measures the DEPLOYED ensemble score only - per-seed and per-trial score surfaces are a separate question.", "priority_rank": 1, "rev": "1", "status": "measured", "summary": "SCORE -> EV/tr SURFACE ON THE FOUR DEPLOYED SYMBOLS (user question: 'just map EV/tr against the score'). Measured on the population that produced the published cells - PERFOLD scores, seed-majority side, frozen labels, no retraining. THE SURFACE, marginal EV/tr by within-fold score percentile (bp): P0-10 -1.64/-1.71/-1.65/-1.51, P50-60 -1.82/-1.83/-1.66/-1.62, P90-95 -2.10/-2.07/-1.67/-1.67, P99-99.9 -2.13/-2.04/-1.57/-2.17, P99.9-99.99 +0.95/-1.35/-0.50/-1.73, TOP 0.01% +19.20/+13.45/+10.34/+12.00 (DOGE/XRP/BTC/ETH; n=343/340/390/392, SE 2.48/2.97/2.24/3.31). SHAPE: the dependency is a STEP, not a proportionality. Over the bottom 99.9% of the score range EV is flat and drifts slightly DOWNWARD as the score rises (-1.6 -> -2.1), and the whole-population rank correlation between score and realised net is -0.0034/-0.0073/-0.0112/-0.0053 - marginally NEGATIVE on all four. Hit rate over that same range is monotonically INCREASING (40% -> 47%): the score orders win-probability cleanly everywhere, but until the extreme top that ordering does not pay for the loss tail. All the economics is in the last hundredths of a percent, and THERE the relation is steep and smooth - DOGE EV(top-q) runs +0.33bp at q=0.30% -> +4.61 at 0.035% -> +17.1 at 0.010% -> +41.8 at 0.0015%. Argmax of EV/tr is the most selective point measurable (50 trades) on every symbol; argmax of bp/day is a separate question and is not this measurement. SECOND RESULT, NOT PREVIOUSLY RECORDED - SCORE LEVELS ARE NOT COMPARABLE ACROSS FOLDS, AND THAT IS LOAD-BEARING. The score is a rank-CDF built on its own fold's train distribution. Selecting the deployed number of trades with ONE global threshold over the test year gives DOGE +4.61 / XRP +15.54 / BTC +8.82 / ETH -4.42; thresholding INSIDE each fold on the same rows gives +9.73 / +12.19 / +10.43 / +10.74. On ETH that is the difference between a negative and a positive cell, and on DOGE it is a factor of 2.1. So the per-fold (FIXQ) / per-day (DYN) construction of tau is not a protocol detail - it carries a large part of the cell. The residual to the published cells (+10.51 / +21.31 / +12.27 / +15.79) is the finer tau construction plus, on XRP and ETH, a different selected set than a flat top-q. CONSISTENCY: EV over all filled rows and the row counts reproduce the untraded-population record exactly (DOGE -1.824bp, hit 42.96%, 3,393,760 filled of 4,191,122), which is the join check. RELATION TO THE OBJECTIVE-GAP RECORD (modelcap-20260731_objective_operating_point_gap): this is the direct picture of why a bulk metric cannot see the operating point - averaging over a range where the surface is flat and slightly negative cannot resolve a step that lives in its last 0.01%. It does NOT by itself say the frozen objective should change; a tail-weighted B objective remains a candidate for its own preregistered tier.", "ts": "2026-08-01T00:20:00Z"}
{"experiment_id": "modelcap-20260801_score_ev_surface_4sym_AMEND1", "hypothesis_id": "MODELCAP", "note": "Runner research/runtime/score_ev_curve.py updated in place: SYMS['ETH'] now carries the safety cell (cell_ev 17.065 / cell_n 295, form 'DYN t5 + HARMONY') with the growth form kept as `alt`, plus a new harmony_diag() that rebuilds cons from the per-seed PERFOLD scores and their own FIXQ taus and reproduces BOTH published ETH cells as its self-check. Artifacts research_runs/strictfill_cells/SCORE_EV_CURVES.{json,html} regenerated; the json now carries a 'harmony' block (growth/safety cells, rows removed, top-q inside the harmony-kept set). The DOGE/XRP/BTC numbers in the regenerated artifacts are byte-identical to the parent run. STILL NOT MEASURED: the same curve under the strict (cell A2) labels, and the harmony overlay's effect on the other three symbols (it was never part of their deployed form).", "priority_rank": 1, "rev": "1", "status": "measured", "summary": "AMENDMENT to modelcap-20260801_score_ev_surface_4sym (user correction, 2026-08-01): THE ETH OPERATING POINT IN THE PARENT RECORD WAS THE WRONG FORM. The parent placed ETH at the GROWTH cell (+15.788bp / 430 trades, no overlay); the ETH instance actually ran engine v4 with HARMONY=1, i.e. the SAFETY form (+17.065 / 295), per trading_algorithm DEPLOYMENTS.md ('harmony filter skips trades with 2..6 of 8 seeds above frozen per-seed taus'). Corrected here and in the artifacts. VERIFICATION, done from the PERFOLD artifacts alone: both ETH forms reproduce to the third decimal - DYN t5 gives +15.788/430 and DYN t5 + HARMONY gives +17.065/295, matching the published pair exactly, which independently confirms the harmony mask transcribed into strictfill_cells.py from axb_engine.rs v4. WHAT THE OVERLAY DOES, MEASURED: on the whole filled population it removes only 464 rows of 3,892,883 (0.012%) - almost every decision has cons=0 seeds above their own frozen tau - but inside the traded set it removes 135 of 430, and EV rises +15.79 -> +17.07 with hit 66.5% -> 69.8%. CONSEQUENCE FOR THE SURFACE, AND IT IS A REAL ONE: HARMONY is not a threshold on the score. It deletes the MIDDLE of the seed-consensus distribution (block when 2 <= cons <= N-2), so the traded set is NOT a prefix of the score ranking and the ETH point is not required to lie on a top-q curve at all - unlike DOGE/XRP/BTC, whose policies are pure thresholds. Quantified: a flat top-q INSIDE the harmony-kept set at the same n=295 gives +10.61 against the traded +17.07, and per-fold top-q over all decisions at that q gives +9.34 (pooled -0.10). So on ETH the score threshold alone reaches roughly +9..+11 and the remaining ~6bp comes from the overlay plus the daily tau. NOTHING ELSE IN THE PARENT RECORD CHANGES: the DOGE/XRP/BTC figures, the step shape, the marginal bands and the per-fold-vs-pooled result are untouched - the ETH marginal band figures were always computed on all decisions and carry no overlay. The parent's own scope line already said 'ETH is the growth form (no HARMONY)', so the record was internally honest but pointed at a cell that is not the one that traded. SECOND CORRECTION, wording: the parent and the figure called all four 'deployed'. They are published deploy-class cells; since 2026-07-26 only DOGE is live, XRP/BTC/ETH are out of live with their VMs stopped.", "ts": "2026-08-01T01:10:00Z"}
{"experiment_id": "objsel-20260802_trial_selection_surface_4sym", "hypothesis_id": "OBJSEL", "rev": 1, "ts": "2026-08-02T00:55:00Z", "status": "measured", "priority_rank": 1, "summary": "OBJSEL rev1 MEASURED - THE TRIAL-SELECTION SURFACE ON THE FOUR DEPLOYED SYMBOLS (prereg followed exactly; no retraining, no new data). Substrate = the MODELCAP capture, 25 B-trials x 6 folds x 4 seeds x 4 symbols = 2400 trial rescores. PARITY GATE PASSED ON ALL FOUR: 600 trials each reproduced the stored search objective, max |d| = 9.29e-11 / 6.69e-11 / 6.92e-11 / 8.35e-11 (DOGE/XRP/BTC/ETH, tol 1e-6), which validates the val-window reconstruction, the vol-norm and the row join. PRIMARY - THE SURFACE (mean over the 4 symbols of the per-cell mean; bracket = across-symbol range). RELIABILITY = Spearman of the metric's own 25-trial ranking between the first and second temporal half of the val window; RELEVANCE = Spearman between the metric on val and the trial's realised TEST EV. q=1.0 (THE INCUMBENT bulk IC): reliability +0.645 [+0.53,+0.74], relevance +0.002 [-0.16,+0.19]. q=0.1: +0.444 / +0.004. q=0.03: +0.206 / -0.024. q=0.01: +0.087 / -0.046. q=0.003: +0.042 / -0.027. q=0.001: +0.020 / -0.016. ev_budget (top-K per val day = the DEPLOYED selection semantics): +0.106 [+0.09,+0.13] / +0.049 [+0.03,+0.06]. SHAPE, AND IT REFUTES THE MOTIVATING SHAPE: reliability falls MONOTONICALLY by ~30x from q=1 to q=0.001, while relevance never leaves zero ANYWHERE on the axis. The prereg hypothesis - that the metric is uninformative because it is measured off the operating point, so relevance should RISE toward the operating point - is NOT supported: moving the metric to the operating point buys no relevance and costs essentially all of the reliability. There is no reliability/relevance trade-off to exploit here; there is a reliability cliff beside a flat-zero relevance line. The incumbent's ORIGINAL stability rationale (HD3 rev4, 'IC computed on ~170k windows -> less val-overfit than AUC/EV') is therefore CONFIRMED and quantified for the first time in the deployed h150 class. Per-symbol relevance for ic_q1 flips sign across symbols (DOGE +0.190+-0.073, BTC -0.160+-0.065) - opposite signs at ~2.5 SE each, the signature of no consistent effect rather than a symbol-conditional one. SECOND RESULT, LARGER THAN THE ONE THE TIER WAS BUILT TO TEST - THE SEARCH IS SAMPLING, NOT SELECTING. Paired per cell, incumbent test EV MINUS the mean over all 25 trials of that cell: DOGE +0.34+-0.94 (t=+0.36), XRP +0.96+-1.17 (t=+0.83), BTC -3.04+-1.89 (t=-1.61), ETH -0.24+-1.47 (t=-0.16); POOLED -0.49+-0.71 bp (t=-0.70). The trial that bulk IC picks is statistically indistinguishable from a trial drawn at random out of the same 25. Meanwhile the choice itself is NOT small: mean per-cell peak-to-peak of test EV across the 25 trials = 19.4 / 25.3 / 16.8 / 27.2 bp (DOGE/XRP/BTC/ETH), against deployed cell magnitudes of +11..+23 bp; per-cell mean oracle (best trial, an in-sample-on-test ceiling, NOT a lever) +8.90/+13.17/+8.74/+18.67 vs incumbent -0.41/+1.44/-2.05/+4.76. So the per-fold 25-trial hyperparameter search injects ~17-27 bp of cell variance and captures none of it. ONLY SURVIVING CANDIDATE, EXPLICITLY UNDER-POWERED: ev_budget is the single metric whose SWITCH (test EV of its pick minus test EV of the incumbent's pick) is positive on all four symbols - +1.15/+0.71/+3.00/+0.57, pooled +1.36+-0.89 bp, t=+1.53, sign-consistency 4/4 (p~0.125). It is also the only metric with positive relevance on all four. NOT significant; recorded as a hypothesis to power, not a result. SCOPE LIMIT, PREREGISTERED AND BINDING ON THE READING: the trial boosters are fit on the subsampled tuning set sb, whereas the deployed Bg is a REFIT on the gated train window carrying the winning HP. The RELIABILITY axis is unaffected (it is computed within val, within trial). The relevance and random-draw results would understate the search if HP acts mainly through the refit - that refit arm requires training and is a separate cell. Every number = cell: symbol x CL-year walk-forward (W200/T30/EMB2, 6 folds) x the deployed h150 policy class x deployed budget (DOGE t10, XRP/BTC/ETH t5) x the frozen-label MODELCAP capture.", "note": "Script research/runtime/objsel_trial_rescore.py (new; built on the logit_anatomy.py load/vol-norm skeleton, causal_rolling copied verbatim from the frozen trainer). Run on xsym-32 (gen-lang-client-0075410383, 30 vCPU, europe-west1-b, same region as the bucket) per the user host directive 2026-08-01; 4 jobs in parallel, OMP_NUM_THREADS=7, ~2.5h wall, RSS 8-9.5GB/job. Artifacts research_runs/objsel/OBJSEL_{DOGE,XRP,BTC,ETH}.json carry every per-trial params/metrics row. ETH: 7 of 600 trials select zero trades (1 cell has a nan incumbent) - excluded pairwise, n=23 for ETH in the paired test. Prior art located and stated in the prereg: scripts/subs60_xgb_optuna_ev.py implements a tail-scored B objective and was never recorded in either ledger; this tier is its first measurement, and the answer is that the tail-scored direction does not pay in this class. FORWARD OPTION SUGGESTED BY THE DATA, NOT PREREGISTERED (user decision): if the trial landscape is unresolvable at this val power, the instrument is averaging rather than arg-maxing. That is not speculation by analogy - MODELCAP rev1 measured that the 4-seed ensemble gain is PURE RANKING DENOISE (DOGE per-seed +8.14 -> ENS +13.35), i.e. the same class of noise, converted into edge by averaging. A TRIAL-ensemble is the directly analogous instrument and is computable on the 2400 already-captured boosters with no retraining."}
{"experiment_id": "objsel-20260802_rev2_hpfix_parity_gates", "hypothesis_id": "OBJSEL", "rev": 2, "ts": "2026-08-02T15:20:00Z", "status": "measured", "priority_rank": 1, "summary": "OBJSEL rev2 PARITY GATES PASSED ON BOTH PROTOCOLS - the HP_FIX opt-in is output-neutral. The gate is the STRONG form: the INC arm was run through the PATCHED trainer with the incumbent's own stored hyperparameters, so passing proves that SKIPPING both 25-trial Optuna studies perturbs neither the RNG stream, nor the fit order, nor any downstream score. Three runs, each 6 folds, compared key-by-key against the stored PERFOLD artifacts: (1) plain v1 (subs60_xgb_optuna_ic.py) + HP_FIX, DOGE S0 vs maker_labels_tb3s_h150anch/PERFOLD_S0_DOGE - 66/66 keys BIT-EXACT; (2) v1cap (the capture variant, used in production so the arm weights are saved per the standing capture-everything directive) + HP_FIX, DOGE S0 - 66/66 BIT-EXACT; (3) v2 (subs60_xgb_sobol_v2.py) + HP_FIX, ETH S0 with DROP_COLS=67,68,69,70 vs maker_labels_tb3s_h150danch_v2notod/PERFOLD_S0_ETH - 66/66 BIT-EXACT. Gate (2) was run specifically because v1cap and the HP_FIX patch had each been certified separately against v1, and two separately gated changes are not the same object as their composition. CONSEQUENCE THAT REMOVES WORK: since the INC arm reproduces the stored artifacts bit-exactly, the INC arm IS the published PERFOLD set and does not need to be computed - the campaign drops from 64 to 48 jobs (MAXEV/MINEV/EVBUD x 4 symbols x 4 seeds). SPEC-CONSTRUCTION CHECK, run before any training: research/runtime/objsel_refit_spec.py rebuilt each cell's incumbent hpB/biB from TRIALS_*_B_index.json and required equality with the hpB/biB stored in MODELS_*_hp.json - 96/96 cells agreed. EVBUD selects a different trial from INC in 91 of 96 cells. METHOD DEFECT FOUND AND FIXED IN THE GATE ITSELF, recorded because it would have produced a FALSE tier failure: the first comparison used np.array_equal, which reports NaN != NaN, so netl/nets (NaN on unfilled windows) came back as differing while the same output already showed ndiff=0. The comparison was moved to a raw BYTE comparison (x.tobytes() == y.tobytes()), which is the actual bit-exactness test and is NaN-correct; 9 of 11 keys had passed under either rule, only the two NaN-carrying float arrays were affected. VERSION-CONTROL GAP CLOSED: subs60_xgb_sobol_v2.py - the trainer that produced the DEPLOYED ETH cell - was NOT in the repository and existed only on the VM (the same class of gap the runtime README records for the economics scripts). It is pulled into scripts/ as part of this tier. HOST/ENV: xsym-32 (gen-lang-client-0075410383, 30 vCPU, europe-west1-b) per the standing directive; nthread=4, FOLD_PAR 3-6 for the gates, FOLD_PAR=1 x 7 slots for the campaign. Relevant to the gate design: the KNOWN_PITFALLS entry 'changing nthread changes low bits' is broader than what is measured - modelcap-20260731 reproduced July artifacts bit-exactly across hosts at nthread 2 vs 4 (12/12 folds), and these gates reproduce at nthread=4 against artifacts built at NTHREAD=2. Not editing the pitfall entry on two data points, but the risk it flags did not materialise here.", "note": "Patches are opt-in and default-off in all three trainers (HP_FIX unset -> every code path unchanged); research/runtime/orchestrate2.py gained an additive ARM mode (arm_job + ARM:SYM:SEED job triples + a per-symbol config table) leaving the legacy (sym,seed) path untouched. Campaign launched 2026-08-02 15:26 UTC, 48 jobs, single orchestrator verified (no duplicate run). Cell computation for the arms is offline from PERFOLD, as strictfill_cells does - perseed/ens are not run in arm mode."}
{"experiment_id": "objsel-20260803_rev1_AMEND1_spread_vs_seed_noise", "hypothesis_id": "OBJSEL", "rev": 1, "ts": "2026-08-03T00:30:00Z", "status": "measured", "priority_rank": 1, "summary": "AMENDMENT to objsel-20260802_trial_selection_surface_4sym (self-correction, prompted by a user question about what to expect from rev2). THE PARENT RECORD OVER-STATED ITS SECOND RESULT. It reported the 25-trial peak-to-peak of test EV (19.4/25.3/16.8/28.0 bp on DOGE/XRP/BTC/ETH) as 'the per-fold search injects ~17-27bp of cell variance', against deployed cell magnitudes of +11..+23bp. That framing does not survive a noise-scale comparison, which the parent should have run and did not. THE COMPARISON, on the SAME rev1 artifacts, no new compute: SEED spread = sd across the 4 seeds of the INCUMBENT cell at fixed fold and fixed selection rule = pure estimator/model noise with NO hyperparameter variation. TRIAL spread = sd across the 25 trials within a cell. Mean over cells (bp): DOGE trial 4.80 vs seed 8.05 (ratio 0.60); XRP 6.00 vs 7.56 (0.79); BTC 4.20 vs 6.96 (0.60); ETH 6.73 vs 9.28 (0.73). The observed trial peak-to-peak is also BELOW what 25 iid draws at the seed noise scale would produce (19.4 vs 31.6; 25.3 vs 29.7; 16.8 vs 27.4; 28.0 vs 36.5). CORRECTED READING: varying the hyperparameters across the whole 25-trial search moves the traded cell LESS than changing the random seed does. The trial-level variation sits INSIDE the noise band the protocol already carries from seeds alone - the band it already handles by averaging 4 seeds into the deployed ensemble. 'The search injects cell variance' is therefore wrong as stated; the search's variation is a sub-dominant noise source. What the parent measured correctly and still stands: bulk IC has reliability +0.645 and relevance +0.002, relevance is zero at every selectivity, and the incumbent trial is indistinguishable from a random draw among the 25 (pooled -0.49+-0.71 bp). CAVEAT STATED AGAINST THIS AMENDMENT'S OWN CONCLUSION: the 25 trials within a cell share the fold, the data and the A model, so their selected trade sets overlap heavily and their EVs are positively correlated - which DEFLATES the trial sd relative to independent draws, while the 4 seeds carry independently trained A and B models. The comparison is therefore not apples-to-apples and part of the 0.60-0.79 ratio is that structure. The direction (trial variation not larger than seed variation) is robust to it; the exact ratio is not. PREREGISTERED EXPECTATION FOR rev2, recorded BEFORE its arms finish so neither outcome can be narrated as expected: (1) EVBUD minus INC ~ 0 and not significant, because a metric with relevance +0.049 selects near-randomly and the incumbent is itself near-random; (2) MAXEV minus MINEV collapses from the ~20bp it holds BY CONSTRUCTION (those arms were selected ON the test outcome, so regression to the mean is guaranteed) to an estimated 0-5bp. rev2's discriminator is that gap, not the EVBUD arm: near zero => hyperparameters do not matter at this data scale and result (b) is restated as 'the cell estimator carries ~5bp of its own error'; still above ~10bp => hyperparameters do matter and are being chosen badly, which would make trial-averaging worth building.", "note": "No new compute; computed from research_runs/objsel/OBJSEL_{SYM}.json. Parent record NOT mutated (append-only) - this amendment supersedes its second headline only, and the first (the reliability x relevance surface) is unchanged. rev2's 48-arm campaign was already running when this was computed and is unaffected by it."}
{"experiment_id": "objsel-20260803_consensus_surface_4sym", "hypothesis_id": "ENSDEC", "rev": 1, "ts": "2026-08-03T03:20:00Z", "status": "measured", "priority_rank": 1, "summary": "THE SEED-CONSENSUS SELECTIVITY SURFACE, 4 SYMBOLS - the second selectivity axis, mapped for the first time. The deployed policies select on ONE axis (ensemble score vs a causal tau); the ETH SAFETY form adds a different one - cons = number of members whose OWN score clears its OWN frozen per-seed tau, with harmony blocking 2 <= cons <= N-2, i.e. keeping BOTH extremes. The ledger held exactly one point on this axis (ETH DYN t5 +15.79/430 without, +17.07/295 with) and no surface. Computed from PERFOLD alone - no retraining, frozen labels; fixq_tau / sel_fixq / sel_dyn / the harmony rule transcribed VERBATIM from strictfill_cells.py and metrics() VERBATIM from strictfill_economics.py, so selection and economics sit on the published methodology. VALIDATION: the reference cells reproduce the published pair exactly (ETH +15.788/430 and +17.065/295). RESULT 1 - EV RISES WITH CONSENSUS, WIN RATE DOES NOT TRACK IT. EV/tr by 'at least k votes' climbs cleanly toward unanimity (XRP +21.31->+37.98; BTC +12.27->+37.01; ETH +15.79->+25.26 at k>=7) but hit-rate does not follow: it dips through the middle and recovers only at the extreme on the 4-member symbols (XRP 66.3->76.7%, BTC 68.8->74.6%), while on ETH the HIGHEST win rate sits at cons=0 (76.5%) and the >=7 branch is 64.8%. Consistent with the program's standing finding that the edge is carried by move SIZE: consensus buys bigger wins, not more frequent ones. RESULT 2 - THE DEPLOYED RULE IS THE WRONG SHAPE. This is a PRE-SPECIFIED split (the two halves of an existing rule), not mining: harmony keeps both branches, and the LOW branch (cons<=1) sits BELOW the no-overlay average on all four symbols - DOGE +7.69+-2.57 vs +10.51, XRP +10.72+-6.03 vs +21.31, BTC +11.65+-1.59 vs +12.27, ETH +13.41+-2.30 vs +15.79 - while the HIGH branch runs 1.24-1.86x the average (+15.17+-2.47 / +26.50+-5.69 / +22.86+-6.75 / +25.26+-9.10). High-minus-low gap ~+11.6bp, same sign 4/4, pooled t~3.1; individually only DOGE clears 2 SE. RESULT 3 - FULL ECONOMICS (4.1 methodology, deployed frac, span from d202). UNANIMITY (cons=N) vs no overlay: DOGE n 1204->328, tpd 7.17->1.95, mo ROI +12.05->+5.22%, Sharpe 4.88->3.72, maxDD -13.66->-5.49%, Calmar 21.32->15.30; XRP 401->73, 2.48->0.45, +8.31->+2.62%, 3.41->2.82, -6.62->-1.16%, Calmar 24.24->31.39; BTC 449->59, 2.72->0.36, +5.19->+2.02%, 2.13->1.81, -10.38->-2.12%, Calmar 8.03->12.80; ETH 430->59, 2.81->0.39, +18.06->+3.12%, 2.68->1.29, -20.17->-8.76%, Calmar 31.35->5.09. THE UNIVERSAL PART IS THE DRAWDOWN: maxDD falls on 4 of 4, by 2.3x-5.7x. THE VARYING PART IS THROUGHPUT and it is what decides Calmar - up on XRP (+30%) and BTC (+59%), down on DOGE and ETH. RESULT 4 - BTC IS THE ONE PARETO CELL IN THE TABLE, and the overlay is NOT deployed there: harmony on BTC improves every axis at once - EV +12.27->+15.25, Sharpe 2.13->2.46, maxDD -10.38->-6.84%, Calmar 8.03->13.96, monthly ROI +5.19->+5.75%. Mechanism is symbol-local: at N=4 the rule blocks exactly cons=2, and on BTC that pocket is -11.52 (n=50) while on XRP the same pocket is +19.74. The pocket-level reading is post-hoc on n=36-50 cells and is NOT offered as a lever; the BTC harmony cell itself is a pre-specified rule and is. SCOPE, binding: two ensemble sizes only (4 on DOGE/XRP/BTC, 8 on ETH), one per-seed tau convention, one model family, members decorrelated ONLY BY SEED. '4 of 4' and '8 of 8' are different operating points - 4/4 keeps 27% of DOGE's trades, 8/8 keeps 14% of ETH's - so ETH's weak unanimity cell is confounded with a much sharper cut and is NOT evidence that more members hurt. A matched consensus FRACTION across symbols was not measured. Per-cons single cells run n=22-73 and their SEs (2.3-9.1bp) are quoted for that reason.", "note": "Script research/runtime/consensus_surface.py (new). Run on xsym-32 while the OBJSEL rev2 arm campaign held the other slots; minutes of CPU, no VM cost of its own. Artifacts research_runs/objsel/CONSENSUS_{SYM}.json carry the base-rate cons histogram, the by-cons and both cumulative tables with SEs, and the four economics variants. Prompted by the user pointing at the harmony overlay as a second kind of selectivity discovered on ETH; feeds ENSDEC rev1."}
{"experiment_id": "objsel-20260803_rev2_refit_arms_4sym", "hypothesis_id": "OBJSEL", "rev": 2, "ts": "2026-08-03T19:10:00Z", "status": "measured", "priority_rank": 1, "summary": "OBJSEL rev2 MEASURED - THE TRIAL SPREAD DOES NOT SURVIVE THE REFIT, AND NO ALTERNATIVE SELECTION BEATS THE INCUMBENT. Prereg followed; both predictions registered in objsel-20260803_rev1_AMEND1 BEFORE the arms reported are confirmed. 48 jobs (3 arms x 4 symbols x 4 seeds x 6 folds), zero failures; the INC arm was not recomputed because the rev2 parity gates proved it reproduces the stored PERFOLD bit-exactly on both protocols. Cells computed from PERFOLD by causal_rolling (frozen trainer function, verbatim) at the deployed budgets - the same construction rev1 used, so the two tiers are like-for-like. PRIMARY - THE FORK RESOLVED IN FAVOUR OF 'THE SPREAD COLLAPSES'. MAXEV minus MINEV, paired per (seed,fold), against the ~20bp those arms hold BY CONSTRUCTION in rev1 (they were selected ON the rev1 test outcome): DOGE +0.47+-2.66 (t=+0.18), XRP +0.96+-4.17 (t=+0.23), BTC +2.64+-1.97 (t=+1.34), ETH +3.85+-3.14 (t=+1.23); POOLED +1.98+-1.55 (t=+1.28). The registered prediction was 0-5bp. So once the winning hyperparameters are refit on the full gated/full train window, the choice moves the traded cell by ~2bp, not ~20bp. CONSEQUENCE, AND IT RETRACTS THIS TIER'S OWN PARENT HEADLINE: objsel-20260802's second result - 'the per-fold search injects ~17-27bp of cell variance and captures none of it' - is an artefact of the sb tuning subsample and does NOT describe the deployed protocol. AMEND1 had already moved the framing on indirect evidence (trial spread smaller than seed spread); this is the direct measurement. The search is EXONERATED on this axis. The first result of the parent - the reliability x relevance surface, bulk IC reliability +0.645 / relevance +0.002, relevance zero at every selectivity - is untouched and still stands. SECONDARY - THE HEAD-TO-HEAD THE USER ASKED FOR. EVBUD minus INC, paired per (seed,fold): DOGE -2.24+-1.77 (t=-1.26), XRP -3.78+-2.33 (t=-1.62), BTC -0.04+-2.30 (t=-0.02), ETH +3.85+-3.59 (t=+1.07); POOLED -0.55+-1.29 (t=-0.43), sign inconsistent 3 negative / 1 positive. No improvement, as registered. rev1's ev_budget candidate (+1.36+-0.89, sign-consistent 4/4) does not reproduce once the models are refit - a clean example of a sign-consistency signal at t=1.5 failing to survive. ARM MEANS (EV/tr over cells): DOGE INC +5.70 vs MAXEV +3.03 / MINEV +2.56 / EVBUD +3.46; XRP +8.24 vs +4.00 / +3.04 / +4.91; BTC +10.73 vs +12.43 / +9.79 / +9.80; ETH +9.78 vs +10.12 / +6.27 / +11.86. NO ARM BEATS INC on the paired tests, and on DOGE/XRP the incumbent leads every alternative outright. Stated with its limit: MAXEV/MINEV are outcome-selected and EVBUD is metric-selected, so none of them is a RANDOM-trial arm - this tier therefore shows 'nothing we tried beats the incumbent', not 'the incumbent beats a random draw under refit', which would need a random arm and was not run. THIRD RESULT, NOT SOUGHT, AND IT RESCOPES ALL OF rev1: the same incumbent cell is +5.70 here (refit Bg, from the stored PERFOLD) against -0.41 in rev1 (the same hyperparameters carried by a TRIAL booster fit on the 200k sb subsample). The refit is worth roughly +6bp on DOGE. Every rev1 trial-level number therefore describes a materially weaker object than the deployed one - the prereg said so as a scope limit, but under-estimated the size of the gap. WHAT CLOSES: direction 1 is closed from both ends - rev1 showed moving the selection metric to the operating point buys no relevance at any selectivity, rev2 shows the hyperparameter choice barely moves the deployed cell anyway. There is no repair to make in the search. The measured headroom sits elsewhere (ENSDEC rev1, and symbol expansion). Every number = cell: symbol x CL-year walk-forward W200/T30/EMB2 x the deployed h150 policy class x deployed budget (DOGE t10, XRP/BTC/ETH t5) x per-seed causal_rolling scoring, frozen labels.", "note": "Readout script research/runtime/objsel_arm_cells.py (new); artifact research_runs/objsel/ARMCELLS.json. Campaign ran on xsym-32 via the orchestrate2 ARM mode, 7 slots x nthread=4, ~7h wall, single orchestrator verified. ETH loses a few pairs (n=20-23) where an arm selected zero trades in a fold; excluded pairwise. VM stopped after the readout."}
{"experiment_id": "bulkedge-20260805_fill_selection_anatomy_DOGE", "hypothesis_id": "BULKEDGE", "note": "Runners (research/runtime/, committed with this record): flip_tax_surface.py, fill_selection_split.py, inside_position_edge.py, adverse_fill_vs_hold.py. Invocations, all local, no VM: SYM=DOGE NSEED=4 LOCAL_DIR=<pf_doge> python flip_tax_surface.py | fill_selection_split.py | inside_position_edge.py ; SYM=DOGE ARCHIVE=<DOGE.npz> python adverse_fill_vs_hold.py. Substrate: gs://market-data-0998ac51/research_runs/maker_labels_tb3s_h150anch/PERFOLD_S{0..3}_DOGE_qm0_f{0..5}.npz (570MB) and .../DOGE.npz (1.75GiB label archive, holds 90/150/240s). adverse_fill_vs_hold.py was PATCHED in place before the run: it assumed `_frozen`-suffixed arrays and the parent archive carries only the unsuffixed frozen set, so STRICT=1 would silently have reported frozen numbers as strict; it now detects which set the archive holds, prints it, and refuses STRICT on a parent archive. Per-fold tables, the normalised-capture table and the deployed-cell attribution were computed ad hoc from the same local artifacts and are reproduced by the numbers in the summary; artifacts FLIPTAX_DOGE.json / FILLSPLIT_DOGE.json / INSIDEPOS_DOGE.json / ADVHOLD_DOGE.json are local only (scratchpad) and NOT uploaded - re-running the four commands regenerates them.", "priority_rank": 1, "rev": 1, "status": "exploratory", "summary": "BULKEDGE rev1 MEASURED - THE ANATOMY OF THE NON-TAIL DECISION, DOGE, no retraining, no new data, no capital. VALIDATION GATE PASSED FIRST: the our-side filled population reproduces fillyear-20260731_untraded_population_value exactly - n=3,393,760, EV -1.824bp, hit 42.96%. Everything below sits on that gate. PRIMARY - THE SURFACE, by within-fold ensemble-score percentile (bands 0-10 / 10-50 / 50-90 / 90-99 / 99-99.9 / 99.9-99.99 / 99.99-100), each band decomposed twice. (A) DIRECTION vs ROUND-TRIP TAX, exact on the rows where both sides would have filled: the directional edge is POSITIVE IN EVERY BAND and monotone - +0.209 / +0.264 / +0.290 / +0.483 / +1.003 / +4.014 / +20.419 bp - against a side-symmetric tax that is ~zero everywhere (+0.057 / +0.072 / +0.063 / +0.023 / -0.112 / -0.129 / +0.299). Pooled: edge +0.3131+-0.0105, tax +0.0593+-0.0021, |move| 10.63bp. Flipping the side is WORSE in every band (pooled EV -1.903 vs -1.824), so the bulk's negativity is not a wrong-direction problem and not a cost problem. NORMALISED CAPTURE (edge / |move|) is the honest statement of how much better the model is in the tail: 3.13 / 3.12 / 2.54 / 3.14 / 4.63 / 13.55 / 54.02 % - flat at ~3% across the whole bulk, then an 18x step in the top 0.1%. (B) THE FILL-ASYMMETRY SPLIT, with the accounting identity EV = w_alone*EV_alone + (1-w_alone)*EV_both asserted per band: the loss lives ENTIRELY in the rows where only our side filled. EV(BOTH) is positive in every band (+0.152 / +0.191 / +0.227 / +0.460 / +1.115 / +4.143 / +20.121); EV(ALONE) is negative in every band (-3.582 / -5.024 / -7.644 / -11.377 / -17.620 / -19.900 / -8.011); and the ALONE SHARE falls monotonically with the score, 48.3% / 36.8% / 26.9% / 21.5% / 17.2% / 13.3% / 7.5%. WHAT THAT SETTLES ABOUT THE TAIL, and it corrects the motivating intuition in one place: the tail is NOT exempt because its adverse fills are milder - per adversely-filled row the tail is 3-6x MORE damaged (-19.9 vs -3.6). It is exempt because such fills are 6x RARER there and because its two-sided population captures 54% of the move instead of 3%. Band EV contributions make it arithmetic: alone -1.729 / -1.849 / -2.057 / -2.449 / -3.028 / -2.646 / -0.604 against both +0.079 / +0.121 / +0.166 / +0.361 / +0.924 / +3.592 / +18.603. ATTRIBUTION OF THE DEPLOYED CELL (flat top-q frame, NOT the deployed FIXQ causal-tau rule - stated because the two frames are not the same object): at top-q 0.035% the filled set is n=1,274, EV +9.185, w_alone 10.0%, EV_alone -17.458, EV_both +12.161. Holding both conditional EVs fixed and swapping in the bulk's 32.0% adverse-fill share gives +2.694. So ~71% (+6.49 of +9.19bp) of what the traded cell earns per trade is ADVERSE-FILL AVOIDANCE, not directional capture. THE A HEAD IS THE AVOIDER, WHICH REVERSES THE SUSPECTED MECHANISM: at matched top-q the deployed AxB ranking selects 10.05% ALONE and +9.185bp, while the A-ablated ranking (noa_te, the same seeds' ensemble scored without the A head) selects 58.07% ALONE and -1.188bp; at q=10% the shares are 21.04% vs 44.96%. So the volatility gate does not drag the adverse fills in - removing it is what drags them in. noA is NOT the deployed policy and nothing about the deployed AxB cell is claimed from it; it is the A-ablated contrast only. SECONDARY, THE EXPLOITATION QUESTION THIS TIER WAS MEANT TO OPEN - AND THE FIRST CHANNEL IS SHUT. Model-free hold sweep on the full 371-day label archive (8,976,874 decisions, both sides pooled, populations defined by the fill flags alone and held FIXED while only the exit moves): EV(ALONE) is -8.239 / -8.200 / -8.244 bp at holds of 90 / 150 / 240s - FLAT to the third digit across a 2.7x change in holding time, while the hit rate rises 19.31 -> 25.46 -> 29.83% and win and loss grow together (+4.65/-11.32 -> +9.80/-15.92). EV(BOTH) is likewise flat, -0.380 / -0.375 / -0.388. READING: the adverse-fill loss is ALREADY PRESENT AT THE FILL. It does not accrue along the path, so no UNCONDITIONAL change of hold length attacks it. WHAT SURVIVES OF THE EXIT CHANNEL, measured separately and CONDITIONAL rather than unconditional: from inside the position, the ensemble's own later opinion still separates forward value - signing the 150s move at row i+k by the position opened at row i, agree minus disagree is +0.681 / +0.720 / +0.790 / +0.748 / +0.732 / +0.766 bp at k = 1 / 2 / 5 / 10 / 25 / 50 rows (~3 / 6 / 15 / 30 / 75 / 150 s), positive in 12 of 12 fold x population cells (+0.24 .. +1.33), and present inside the ALONE population itself - which matters because a decision taken from inside the position is free of entry fill-selection BY CONSTRUCTION. SCALE IT HONESTLY: ~+0.7bp of separation against an -8.2bp problem, i.e. a conditional exit can address order-10% of the damage, not the damage. FOLD-LEVEL ROBUSTNESS, run because the pooled numbers hide it: EV(ALONE) is negative in 6/6 folds (-4.68 .. -8.77) - the headline is rock-solid; the directional edge is positive in 6/6 (+0.001 .. +0.601) but small and variable; the TAX is fold-unstable (+0.411 / +0.343 / +0.306 / +0.189 / -0.177 / -1.126), so the pooled +0.059 is a mean over a swinging quantity; and EV(BOTH) is SIGN-INCONSISTENT, negative in 3 of 6 folds (-0.292 / -0.010 / -0.305 / +0.245 / +0.680 / +1.727). That last one is a caveat against this record's own most quotable line: 'the two-sided population is profitable' is NOT established - it is approximately break-even with fold-scale swings, and only its SCORE-CONDITIONAL top end is clearly positive. NOTE ON PRIOR ART: four uncommitted 2026-08-04 scripts asserted the edge/tax and ALONE/BOTH results in their docstrings with no ledger record, no commit and no surviving artifact. This record re-measured them from the published PERFOLD artifacts under the gate; the edge/tax and split reproduce, and this tier adds the per-fold stability, the normalised capture, the deployed-cell attribution, the A-ablation read and the hold sweep. CONFIRMATORY-GATE ANNOTATION (secondary, HM1 s5): none of this is a deploy claim; no capital action, no policy change, the live DOGE instance is untouched. LIMITS OF THE CELL: DOGE only, h150-anchored protocol, frozen labels (the entry-fill model that OVER-FILLS - the strict relabel was not run here), 4 seeds x 6 folds test year for the PERFOLD parts vs the full 371 days for the archive part (which is why archive ALONE is -8.24 pooled over both sides while the PERFOLD our-side test-fold figure is -6.25 - different populations, not a discrepancy); ALONE/BOTH is a POST-FILL classification and is therefore NOT directly selectable ex ante, which is exactly why the A-head and inside-position reads are the ones that carry exploitation weight.", "ts": "2026-08-05T09:30:00Z"}
{"experiment_id": "bulkedge-20260805_rev1_AMEND1_deployed_cell_frame", "hypothesis_id": "BULKEDGE", "note": "SYM=DOGE NSEED=4 BUDGET=10 LOCAL_DIR=<pf_doge> python fill_selection_split.py. Same PERFOLD substrate as the parent. The 9.9% figure is close to the 10.05% the parent proxy reported for the ALONE share, which is why the share statement held while the attribution magnitude did not - the counterfactual depends on the conditional EVs, and those differ between the frames (-17.458/+12.161 on flat top-q vs -11.833/+12.964 on FIXQ).", "priority_rank": 1, "rev": 1, "status": "exploratory", "summary": "AMENDMENT to bulkedge-20260805_fill_selection_anatomy_DOGE (user challenge, 2026-08-05: was the split measured on the DEPLOYED cell - EV/tr +10.51, FIXQ t10 - or on a proxy?). THE PARENT USED A PROXY AND ITS HEADLINE ATTRIBUTION NUMBER IS WRONG. The parent attributed the traded cell on a FLAT TOP-Q 0.035% frame (n=1,274, EV +9.185) and reported that ~71% of the per-trade EV is one-sided-fill avoidance. A flat top-q is NOT the deployed rule: FIXQ freezes a validation quantile and therefore REDISTRIBUTES trades across days rather than taking a fixed prefix of the score ranking (HD5 rev1 - 69-86% of days get no trade at all), so the two sets are different objects. RE-MEASURED ON THE DEPLOYED SELECTION, with sel_fixq/fixq_tau/KDAYS=30 transcribed verbatim from strictfill_cells.py and the per-fold frozen tau computed from that fold own train scores: GATE PASSED EXACTLY - selected 1,424, filled n=1,204, EV +10.513bp, hit 62.96%, reproducing h1fixedtau-20260712_cl_year to the third decimal. THE SPLIT ON THAT SET: ALONE n=119 (9.9% of the traded set) at -11.833bp; BOTH n=1,085 at +12.964bp. COUNTERFACTUAL, holding the cell own conditional EVs fixed and swapping in the bulk 32.0% one-sided share: +5.039bp. CORRECTED ATTRIBUTION: +5.475 of the +10.513bp - i.e. 52%, not 71% - is avoidance of the one-sided fill, the remaining 48% being the cell far better directional capture. The DIRECTION of the parent claim survives (about half the traded edge is fill selection, not prediction) and its magnitude does not; the parent number is retracted. The parent surface, per-fold stability, A-ablation and hold-sweep results are computed on their own frames and are untouched. RUNNER: the deployed-cell section was added IN PLACE to research/runtime/fill_selection_split.py (env BUDGET, default 10) rather than as a new script, so the gate travels with the analysis.", "ts": "2026-08-05T12:10:00Z"}
{"experiment_id": "bulkedge-20260805_rev1_AMEND2_immediate_entry_band", "hypothesis_id": "BULKEDGE", "note": "SYM=DOGE NSEED=4 BUDGET=10 LOCAL_DIR=<pf_doge> ARCHIVE=<DOGE.npz> python research/runtime/immediate_entry_band.py. Artifact IMMEDIATE_DOGE.json local only. The bpd comparison holds per-trade notional fixed and assumes the 22.3/day band fits the 50-slot pool at a 60s hold (peak concurrency not modelled) - it is a bp/day ratio, not a full 4.1 economics run.", "priority_rank": 1, "rev": 1, "status": "exploratory", "summary": "AMENDMENT 2 to bulkedge-20260805_fill_selection_anatomy_DOGE (user question, 2026-08-05: take band 99.9-99.99 where there IS edge, assume we enter the moment B says long/short, by what % would the deployed cell ROI change?). NEW INSTRUMENT, because the maker artifacts CANNOT answer it: netl/nets exist only where that side FILLED, so the signed move (netl-nets)/2 - the quantity every edge number in the parent is built from - is computable ONLY on both-filled rows, which are selected FOR being two-sided. The label archive rH15/rH30/rH60 (TIME-based forward mid log-returns in bp, +-5s tolerance, defined for EVERY decision regardless of fill) carry no fill selection at all. Runner research/runtime/immediate_entry_band.py, three gates: day-join equals PERFOLD day_te, archive fl/fs/pnl equal PERFOLD arrays, and the deployed FIXQ t10 cell reproduces +10.513bp / n=1204 - all PASSED. UNIT TRAP RECORDED: rh_time already multiplies by 1e4, so rH is ALREADY bp; the first run scaled again and produced moves of -1438..+74917 bp, i.e. 14%-750% in 15 seconds. Absurd on sight, and the reason to state units in the docstring of the producing function. ANSWER TO THE QUESTION: THE ROI WOULD FALL, NOT RISE. Band 99.9-99.99 has 3,772 decisions = 22.3/day against the deployed 1,204 trades = 7.1/day. GROSS signed mid move, NO execution cost of any kind: -0.051bp at 15s, +1.028bp at 30s, +1.739bp at 60s (hit 49.0 / 51.1 / 53.1%). Gross bp/day: -1.13 / +22.94 / +38.82 against the deployed +74.90 bpd - a ratio of -0.02x / 0.31x / 0.52x. So even at ZERO cost the band delivers at most about half the deployed cell bp/day; the break-even cost is NEGATIVE (-1.62bp at 60s), i.e. no execution cost makes the switch match the incumbent. A taker round trip costs several bp, which takes the band negative outright. Same computation on the DEPLOYED selection itself: entering those 1,424 decisions immediately is worth +6.075bp gross at 60s = 51.19 bpd = 0.68x of what the maker route earns net at 150s - the resting quote entry is itself worth several bp of price improvement, which an immediate entry gives away. THE RESULT THAT CORRECTS THE PARENT FRAMING, and it is the important one. Measured UNCONDITIONALLY, the signed 60s mid move by band is -0.178 / -0.198 / -0.244 / -0.337 / -0.159 / +1.739 / +7.492 - NEGATIVE over the whole bulk and positive only in the top 0.1%. The parent reported the directional edge as positive in EVERY band (+0.209 .. +20.419); that statement is TRUE ONLY WITHIN THE BOTH-FILLED SUBPOPULATION and does not generalise, and this record retracts the generalised reading of it. The parent did label the quantity both-filled-only, but led with it as if it were the bulk direction. THE MECHANISM, now visible unconditionally - the fill-selection identity, signed 60s move by band x what the resting quote would have done: ALONE -3.515 / -4.863 / -7.395 / -10.994 / -17.237 / -24.322 / -43.709; BOTH +0.216 / +0.277 / +0.372 / +0.535 / +0.720 / +1.753 / +6.611; UNFILLED (the quote never traded) +3.207 / +4.916 / +7.806 / +11.687 / +18.566 / +26.982 / +37.497. The ALONE and UNFILLED legs are near mirror images at every band. THAT IS THE USER ORIGINAL MECHANISM MEASURED WITHOUT ANY MODEL: when the price moves our way the resting quote is left behind and we are NOT in the trade; when it moves against us we ARE. But it also bounds the hypothesis - the mirror is close to symmetric, so the unconditional move is ~0 and slightly negative, meaning the bulk holds no positive mid-to-mid directional value to harvest at 15-60s. What the tail has is a genuinely positive unconditional move (+1.7 / +7.5bp), not merely a lower adverse-fill share. NO CAPITAL, NO POLICY CHANGE; the live DOGE instance is untouched. LIMITS: DOGE only; the archive longest forward return is 60s while the deployed hold is 150s, so an immediate entry is priced only to 60s; rH is mid-to-mid and therefore an upper bound on any executable version of it.", "ts": "2026-08-05T15:40:00Z"}
{"experiment_id": "bulkedge-20260805_rev1_AMEND3_immediate_entry_150s", "hypothesis_id": "BULKEDGE", "note": "research/runtime/immediate_entry_band.py extended in place with the chain gate, the hop-tolerance sweep and the paired 150s section; the 60s unpaired tables it still prints are kept as the diagnostic that motivated the fix, not as the answer. Same invocation as AMEND2.", "priority_rank": 1, "rev": 1, "status": "exploratory", "summary": "AMENDMENT 3, and it CORRECTS AMEND2 (user correction, 2026-08-05: the deployed cell holds 150s FROM THE FILL, not 60s from the decision). AMEND2 priced the immediate entry at 60s because that is the archive longest rH leg, and compared it against a 150s incumbent - two different objects. FIX: the 150s move is CHAINED over ts, r150(i) = rH60(i) + rH60(j60) + rH30(j120) with j60/j120 the decision rows nearest ts_i+60s / ts_i+120s (same day, within HOP_TOL). CHAIN GATE PASSED: chained rH30(i)+rH30(j30) reproduces the direct rH60(i) on n=8,221,210 - means -0.0130 vs -0.0120, corr 0.9835, sd(diff) 2.26bp (the join gap, mean-zero). SECOND DEFECT FOUND AND FIXED IN THE SAME PASS: r150 coverage FALLS WITH THE SCORE - 0.92 in the bottom decile against 0.46 on the deployed set at the original +-5s hop tolerance - so AMEND2 unpaired means over covered rows were a score-biased subsample. Tolerance swept (5/15/30/60s); coverage stabilises by +-15s at 0.75-0.81 on the tail bands and every immediate-vs-maker number is now PAIRED on identical rows. CORRECTED ANSWER TO THE USER QUESTION. Band 99.9-99.99, entering immediately and holding 150s, GROSS mid-to-mid with NO execution cost: +4.040bp per decision, hit 57.03%, on 16.7 priceable decisions/day of 22.3 in the band = +67.49 bpd against the deployed +74.90 bpd, i.e. 0.90x. If the 25% of band rows that cannot be priced are worth what the priced ones are, full throughput gives 22.3 x 4.040 = 90.1 bpd = 1.20x. So the honest range at ZERO cost is 0.9-1.2x - COMPARABLE to the incumbent, not the 0.31-0.52x AMEND2 reported. AMEND2 magnitude is retracted; it was the horizon error plus the coverage bias, both in the same direction. THE COST BUDGET IS WHAT DECIDES IT, and it is small: matching the deployed +74.90 bpd on 22.3 trades/day needs +3.36bp net per trade against +4.040 gross, so the whole round-trip execution budget is +0.68bp. Crossing the spread on DOGE alone is of that order before any taker fee, so the switch does not clear the incumbent on any realistic cost - but it is a near-miss, not the 3x shortfall AMEND2 implied. THE OTHER AMEND2 CLAIM THAT DOES NOT SURVIVE PAIRING: AMEND2 said the resting-quote entry is itself worth several bp of price improvement, from an unpaired 0.68x. PAIRED on identical rows the two routes are indistinguishable - FIXQ t10 immediate +8.691 vs maker +8.455, diff +0.236 +-0.588; band 99.9-99.99 +1.133 vs +1.121, diff +0.012 +-0.250; band 99.99-100 -1.366 +-1.043. The entry mechanism is NOT where the value is. Retracted. In the BULK the paired diff is small but significantly POSITIVE for the immediate route (+0.084 +-0.010 / +0.096 +-0.005 / +0.128 +-0.006 / +0.114 +-0.014 over bands 0-10 / 10-50 / 50-90 / 90-99) - while BOTH routes are worth -1.5 to -1.9bp there, so it improves nothing worth having. WHAT STANDS FROM AMEND2 UNCHANGED: the unconditional fill-selection identity (ALONE -3.5..-43.7 vs UNFILLED +3.2..+37.5 at 60s, near mirror images at every band) and the retraction of the parent generalised edge-positive-everywhere claim. LIMITS: DOGE only; r150 is a chained estimate carrying ~2.3bp of join noise per row (SE ~0.05bp at band n); mid-to-mid, hence an upper bound on anything executable; 25-31% of tail rows unpriceable and assumed representative where stated.", "ts": "2026-08-05T18:20:00Z"}
{"experiment_id": "ops_outage-20260805_gcp_billing_closed_all_live_stopped", "hypothesis_id": "OPS-EXEC", "note": "No capital action taken and none possible - the exchange side is untouched, the position state is whatever the engine left. Restart path is recovery, not a deploy decision: prefer reactivating or upgrading 01E3AA (may preserve the trial credit), fallback a new billing account re-linked to project-0998ac51 (same static IP 35.221.108.194, no data migration, credit forfeited). billing.admin on 01E3AA is held by virginship06@, Delmiron27@ and virgin.ship03@. FLAT-CHECK before restarting axb-exec-doge. Weights, tau-seed prefixes and unit files are unaffected by the outage.", "priority_rank": 1, "rev": 1, "status": "measured", "summary": "OUTAGE RECORD, not an experiment. ALL LIVE TRADING AND THE 24/7 RECORDER STOPPED on 2026-08-05 when the GCP billing account funding project-0998ac51 entered state CLOSED. Not a crash, not an exchange event, not a policy or research decision. EVIDENCE: GCS reads on market-data-0998ac51 return 403 with Google text \"The billing account for the owning project is disabled in state closed\"; gcloud billing projects describe reports billingEnabled: false; the Compute API refuses even  for the same reason, so the VM state CANNOT BE READ and is recorded as unverified. WHAT WENT DOWN: axb-engine-doge, axb-exec-doge and the co-located recorder, all on VM scalper-recorder (asia-northeast1-b). STOP TIME IS A WINDOW, DELIBERATELY: last successful bucket read completed 2026-08-05 08:59:04 UTC (a 1.75GiB label-archive download in this session); first billing-closed 403 carries Google response header Wed, 05 Aug 2026 21:31:56 GMT. GCS and GCE enforcement are separate paths, so the instance may have stopped anywhere in that window or earlier. To be pinned from Console + the exchange last fill once billing is restored; do not quote a point timestamp until then. SCOPE OF THE BILLING FAILURE: all four billing accounts visible from both credentialed Google accounts are OPEN=False (018133-BBEBCE-A6335A, 01CB22-236825-287C72, 01E3AA-9C05AA-66F1C1, 018F84-0D48C4-C8D41C), and gen-lang-client-0075410383 - the heavy-compute project of the standing directive - is billingEnabled: false as well, so NO GCP compute or bucket read is available to this program at all. Re-linking to another EXISTING account cannot help. USER ACCOUNT OF THE CAUSE (their statement, unverified by us and unverifiable through the API): the prepayment Google required to unlock the Free Trial was officially reclaimed; the card is still valid and ~27 of trial credit still displays as Available, but credits are spendable only by an OPEN billing account. DAMAGE, in the order that matters: (1) the recorder gap is PERMANENT - the recorder is the only writer of the live stream, Cryptolake has lapsed, and no vendor sells this back; (2) market-data-0998ac51 is on a deletion clock - it holds PERFOLD, the year label archives, the 371 h2_dir10 dailies and research_runs/deploy_h150/DOGE/seed{0..3} weights, and GCP may delete a billing-disabled project's resources after a grace period on the order of 30 days, so restoring billing is a DATA-PRESERVATION action before it is a trading one; (3) stopped time is live-vs-sim anchor observation not taken, and OPS-EXEC rev14 (USDC fill layer on the full population) is open on exactly that anchor. RESEARCH CONSEQUENCE FOR THE OPEN TIER: BULKEDGE rev2 (the rolling 3s continuation rule the user specified) is BLOCKED but NOT expensive - it needs no rebuild, only the 371 h2_dir10 daily {ts,mid,bid0,ask0} files (~210MB) that already exist in the bucket, plus the PERFOLD scores already held locally. It resumes the moment the bucket reads again. MIRROR: trading_algorithm DEPLOYMENTS.md updated in the same change-window per the deploy-showcase ritual (commit 1b778e9) with the same window, cause, damage ordering and restart path.", "ts": "2026-08-05T22:10:00Z"}
{"experiment_id": "ops_outage-20260805_AMEND1_text_repair", "hypothesis_id": "OPS-EXEC", "note": "No research or operational content changes. The outage record itself stands as written.", "priority_rank": 3, "rev": 1, "status": "measured", "summary": "TEXT REPAIR to ops_outage-20260805_gcp_billing_closed_all_live_stopped. The parent record was appended through a shell command in which backticks were interpreted as command substitution, so one quoted command name was swallowed and the parent now reads 'the Compute API refuses even  for the same reason'. The missing words are 'a plain instances-list call'. Nothing else in the parent was affected - the clause meaning (the Compute API is behind the same billing block, so the VM state cannot be read) is unchanged, and no number, timestamp or conclusion was touched. The parent is NOT edited, per the append-only rule. METHOD NOTE worth keeping: append ledger rows from a FILE, never from an inline double-quoted shell string, or shell metacharacters silently rewrite the record.", "ts": "2026-08-05T22:25:00Z"}
